We had one during our testing period and it has ended. Ally now starts at Starter, Rs 199 for one month.

Starter is a one-off payment. You are not signing up to anything and nothing renews -- when the month is up, it is up. Plus and Pro are monthly plans that do renew, until you cancel.

If you were using Ally free while we were testing, thank you -- and please get in touch if anything about your account looks wrong.', 'walked', 'answered_pending_product_change', 'false', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-06', 'Team decision 2026-09-06. Starter: Rs 199 paid ONCE, buying one month -- it does not auto-renew. Plus (Rs 450) and Pro (Rs 999) are monthly subscriptions, with 12 months for the price of 10 if paid annually. A discovery call is Rs 300 per 30 minutes on any plan. GST is included in every price shown.', NULL, 'HELD until PUBLIC_LAUNCH is on -- describes the paid-only launch state. REVISED 2026-09-06: Starter is a one-off payment for a month, not a monthly subscription. The 2026-09-05 draft said it renewed monthly.', 'group-13-plans-and-what-you-get.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('155', '13', 'plans-and-what-you-get', 'Plans and what you get', 'What happens at the end of my free month?', 'There is no free month, so nothing ends that way.

Ally starts at Starter, Rs 199 for one month, paid once. Plus and Pro are monthly and renew until you cancel.

If you were on our free testing plan, that period has finished. Your data is untouched -- your report, your Founder DNA and everything else are exactly where you left them. Choosing a plan opens them again.

Nothing is deleted because you did not pick a plan straight away.', 'walked', 'answered_pending_product_change', 'false', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-06', 'Team decision 2026-09-06. Starter: Rs 199 paid ONCE, buying one month -- it does not auto-renew. Plus (Rs 450) and Pro (Rs 999) are monthly subscriptions, with 12 months for the price of 10 if paid annually. A discovery call is Rs 300 per 30 minutes on any plan. GST is included in every price shown.', NULL, 'HELD until PUBLIC_LAUNCH is on -- describes the paid-only launch state. REVISED 2026-09-06: Starter is a one-off payment for a month, not a monthly subscription. The 2026-09-05 draft said it renewed monthly.', 'group-13-plans-and-what-you-get.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('156', '13', 'plans-and-what-you-get', 'Plans and what you get', 'What exactly is locked on my plan right now, and why?', 'Your billing page is the honest answer — it shows your plan and what it includes, rather than making you work it out.

Broadly: everyone gets the diagnosis, the report, and the ability to request a call. Talking to Ally, your Next steps, Goals and Plan Your Day come with Plus. Vision, Recommendations, asking Ally about our wider knowledge, email updates and priority calls come with Pro.

Two things are worth saying plainly. Nothing is locked to make you upgrade mid-task — the gates sit at whole features, not inside them. And a locked page tells you it is locked rather than quietly doing less.', 'generated', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-05', 'Gating is per-feature and enforced server-side; the UI mirrors it. Locked navigation items are marked rather than hidden.', NULL, NULL, 'group-13-plans-and-what-you-get.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('157', '13', 'plans-and-what-you-get', 'Plans and what you get', 'Is there a plan for two founders, or a whole team?', 'No. Every plan is for one founder and one business.

There is no team plan, no shared account and no second seat. Two founders means two accounts, each with their own diagnosis.

That is not only a billing decision. The diagnosis is built around one founder -- how you think, how you decide, where you get stuck -- so a shared login would give you a report about neither of you.

If you and your cofounder both want one, the honest answer is to do it separately and then compare. Reading the two side by side tends to be the interesting part.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-06', 'Team decision 2026-09-06: team, cofounder and multi-business accounts are not available. Confirmed in the product: one account is one founder and one business throughout -- profile, diagnosis, report and goals.', NULL, 'Team decision, 2026-09-06.', 'group-13-plans-and-what-you-get.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('158', '13', 'plans-and-what-you-get', 'Plans and what you get', 'Is there a discount for very early-stage founders or students?', NULL, 'policy', 'open_for_team', 'false', 'With the team. No discount mechanism exists in the catalog at all -- not a coupon, not a reduced tier, not a student rate. Adding one is a build as well as a decision, so ''we might'' is not an answer that can be given yet.', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'group-13-plans-and-what-you-get.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('159', '13', 'plans-and-what-you-get', 'Plans and what you get', 'Do you do an annual plan?', 'Yes. Pay for a year and you get two months free.

Choose 12 months on Plus or Pro and you pay for ten. It works out to the same plan, two months cheaper.

Starter works differently -- it is a one-off payment for a month, not a subscription, so there is nothing to buy a year of.

GST is included in every price you see, so the figure on the plans page is the figure you pay.', 'walked', 'answered_pending_product_change', 'false', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-06', 'Team decision 2026-09-06: annual billing is 12 months for the price of 10. GST is included in all plan prices.', 'Annual billing does not exist in the catalog. Every tier is priced monthly and nothing supports a 12-month cycle or a 2-month discount. This answer describes a policy the product cannot yet honour -- it must not publish until annual billing is actually built.', 'HELD until annual billing is built. See the finding.', 'group-13-plans-and-what-you-get.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('160', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'What is a credit?', 'A credit is how we measure your conversations with Ally.

A typical message and its reply costs about two or three credits. A long question, a detailed answer, or one where Ally reads a file you attached will cost more.

Your plan comes with a number of credits each month, and they refresh with it. Your billing page shows how many you have left.

You do not have to manage them day to day. For most founders they simply last the month.', 'generated', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-05', 'One credit is 1,000 tokens; a measured exchange is about 2,400 tokens.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('161', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'What''s the difference between a credit and a token?', 'A token is how AI systems measure text — very roughly, a word and a bit. A credit is our unit, and one credit is a thousand tokens.

You will mostly see credits, because they are a size worth thinking about. Tokens turn up in your daily allowance.

If you would rather not think about either: a message and reply is about two or three credits, and your billing page shows what is left.', 'generated', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-05', 'TOKENS_PER_CREDIT is 1,000. Daily ceilings are expressed in tokens; plan allowances in credits.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('162', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'Why are you measuring me in tokens? I don''t know what a token is.', 'That is fair — most people have no reason to know.

The honest reason is that tokens are what the AI itself charges by, so it is the only measure that does not quietly misprice things. If we counted whole messages instead, a one-word question and a two-page one would cost the same, and one of those would be subsidising the other.

You should not have to care, though. Your billing page shows what is left without you doing any arithmetic, and a typical message costs two or three credits.', 'generated', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-05', 'Metering is token-based end to end; credits are the presentation layer over it.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('163', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'Why did one message cost more than another?', 'Because length is what costs, not the number of messages.

A short question with a short answer costs little. A long question, a reply that goes into detail, or one where Ally had to read a document you attached all cost more.

Attaching a file is the biggest single jump. Ally has to read it before it can answer, and that reading is part of the cost.

So if you are making an allowance last, shorter and more specific questions go a good deal further.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/ally-chat}', '2026-09-05', 'Both the message and the reply are metered, and extracted attachment text is added to the prompt before the model sees it.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('164', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'Where do I see how much I have left?', 'Go to Profile and look at Subscription and billing.

It shows your plan, how much of today''s allowance you have used, and how many diagnoses you have used.

Two different things are worth telling apart there. Your daily allowance starts again each day. Your monthly credits refresh when your plan does.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing,/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'The panel renders ''Talk to Ally — n / limit today'' and ''AI Business Diagnosis — n / 1 lifetime''.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('165', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'Where do I see what I''ve used this month?', 'The same place — Profile, then Subscription and billing.

It shows today''s usage against your daily allowance, and where you are against your plan''s credits.

What it does not show is a message-by-message breakdown. If a large amount went somewhere and you want to know where, ask support and we can look it up for you.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-05', 'Usage is stored per day and per source. No per-message statement is exposed to founders.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('166', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'I still have credits but it says I''ve hit my limit. Which is it?', 'Both are true. They are two different limits and you can meet either one first.

Your daily allowance caps how much you can use in a single day. Your credits are the monthly total.

If you hit the daily one, your credits are untouched and still waiting — you carry on tomorrow.

If you hit the credit one, the month''s allowance is spent.

We know having two is confusing. Your billing page shows both, so you can see which one stopped you.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-05', 'The daily ceiling and the credit balance are separate gates producing different refusals.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('167', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'When does the daily limit reset, and in which timezone?', 'At midnight, India time.

It used to roll over at midnight UTC, which meant founders here got their allowance back at half past five in the morning. Someone who ran out at nine in the evening was told to wait for midnight, and then found nothing there until dawn. That is fixed.

There is no job to wait for either. The moment the date changes, the new day''s allowance is simply there.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-05', 'USAGE_RESET_TIMEZONE is Asia/Kolkata. Usage is keyed by local date rather than reset by a scheduled job, so a new day is a new counter.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('168', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'Do my credits expire?', 'The ones that come with your plan do. They are for that month and do not stack up.

Any credits we have added to your account by hand — to make up for a problem, say — do not expire. Those stay until you use them.

When you spend, the expiring ones go first. That is deliberate: the credits with a deadline get used before the ones without, so you do not lose an allowance while sitting on a gift.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-05', 'Two buckets: plan credits expire at renewal, granted credits do not. Deductions drain the monthly bucket first.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('169', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'I''m on Free — do I get credits again next month?', 'There is no free plan any more, so there is no monthly free grant.

Credits come with a paid plan. Plus gives you 105 a month and Pro gives you 240, and those refresh each month when the plan renews.

Starter has no credits, because it does not include chatting with Ally -- it is the diagnosis and your report, for a one-off Rs 199.

Anything you have already used Ally for is unaffected. Credits control new conversations, never access to what you already have.', 'walked', 'answered_pending_product_change', 'false', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-06', 'Team decision 2026-09-06. Starter: Rs 199 paid ONCE, buying one month -- it does not auto-renew. Plus (Rs 450) and Pro (Rs 999) are monthly subscriptions, with 12 months for the price of 10 if paid annually. A discovery call is Rs 300 per 30 minutes on any plan. GST is included in every price shown.', NULL, 'HELD until PUBLIC_LAUNCH is on -- describes the paid-only launch state. REVISED 2026-09-06: Starter is a one-off payment for a month, not a monthly subscription. The 2026-09-05 draft said it renewed monthly.', 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('170', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'Do unused messages carry over?', 'No. Your monthly credits are for that month and start fresh at each renewal.

Your daily allowance works the same way — it does not build up if you skip a day.

So there is no benefit to saving them. If there is something you have been meaning to ask Ally, asking is free in the sense that holding back does not buy you anything later.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-05', 'Plan credits expire at the renewal boundary; the daily counter is keyed by date and does not accumulate.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('171', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'I''ve run out of messages. What now?', 'It depends which limit you reached, and your billing page shows which.

If it was the daily one, nothing is lost. You carry on tomorrow with a full day''s allowance.

If it was your monthly credits, the options are to wait for your renewal or move to a plan with a larger allowance.

One thing that is never affected: your report, your Founder DNA and everything already in your account stay exactly where they are. Running out stops new conversations, not access to what you have.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-05', 'Both refusals block new chat only. Nothing already stored becomes unreachable.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('172', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'Can I buy more without subscribing?', 'Not at the moment, sorry. There is no way to buy a one-off top-up of credits on its own.

If you need more, the way to get it today is a plan with a larger monthly allowance. Your billing page shows what each one includes.

A top-up is something we have considered rather than something we offer. If it is what you actually want, please tell us — knowing that people are asking is what moves it up the list.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing,/app/feedback}', '2026-09-05', 'A top-up price and credit amount exist as constants but there is no purchase path anywhere in the product, and checkout is not built.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('173', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'Does the diagnosis eat into my allowance?', 'No, not at all. The diagnosis is not metered.

That is deliberate. Nobody should hit a wall halfway through answering questions about their own business, so it is limited by count instead — one per account — rather than by how much you use.

Answer at whatever length you like. Longer, more honest answers make the report better and cost you nothing.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/diagnosis}', '2026-09-05', 'The diagnosis is deliberately absent from the metered sources and bounded by a lifetime count instead.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('174', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'Does generating the report cost me anything?', 'No. The report comes with the diagnosis, and neither is metered.

Downloading it as a PDF, sharing it, and coming back to read it again months later are all free too.

The only thing that uses your allowance is talking to Ally in chat.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/report}', '2026-09-05', 'Report generation, PDF export and share links are outside the metered path entirely.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('175', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'Does uploading a file cost credits?', 'Yes. Ally has to read the file before it can answer, and that reading comes out of your chat allowance.

A long document costs more than a short one.

If you are watching your allowance, it helps to say which part matters. "Look at the pricing section" is cheaper than attaching forty pages and asking what Ally thinks — and it usually gets you a better answer as well.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/ally-chat,/app/billing}', '2026-09-05', 'Extracted attachment text is added to the prompt and metered with the message. The billing panel states this explicitly.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('176', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'Chat has run out. Can I still plan my day?', 'Yes. Planning is not affected by your chat allowance at all.

Adding tasks, setting times, ticking things off and looking at your goals do not use it, because none of them need Ally to think about anything.

So even with chat completely used up for the day, your plan still works normally. That is on purpose — running out of one part of Ally should never take the rest down with it.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/plan}', '2026-09-05', 'Chat and planning meter separately by source. Planning''s counter reads zero because adding a task is deterministic and makes no model call.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('177', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'Does Plan Your Day have its own limit?', 'In practice, no. Planning does not use up anything today.

There is a separate budget set aside for it, kept apart from chat so that running out of one can never disable the other. Nothing currently draws on it, because adding and completing tasks does not need Ally to think.

So plan as much as you like. The only thing your allowance limits is talking to Ally.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/plan}', '2026-09-05', 'planning has its own metered source; the counter is zero in practice. The budget exists so reminder or notification model work has somewhere to land later without a schema change.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('178', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'Roughly how many messages a day does my plan give me?', 'It depends on your plan and on how long your messages are, so the real answer is on your billing page rather than here.

As a rough guide, a typical message and reply costs two or three credits. Long questions, detailed answers and attached documents cost more.

Your billing page shows today''s usage against your allowance, so after a day or two of normal use you will have a much better sense of it than any number we could print.', 'generated', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-05', 'Deliberately no per-plan figure: daily ceilings differ by tier and are changing with the new pricing.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('179', '14', 'credits-tokens-limits', 'Credits, tokens and limits', 'Can I see what a message will cost before I send it?', 'No, and it is a fair thing to want.

The cost depends on how long your message is and how long Ally''s reply turns out to be, and the reply does not exist until it has been written. So there is nothing honest we could show you beforehand.

What you can do is watch the running total on your billing page, which updates as you go.

If a rough "this will cost about this much" would genuinely help you, tell us.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing,/app/feedback}', '2026-09-05', 'Metering happens after the model replies, since output tokens are part of the cost. No pre-flight estimate exists.', NULL, NULL, 'group-14-credits-tokens-limits.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('180', '15', 'paying-invoices-cancelling', 'Paying, invoices, cancelling', 'Is my card charged automatically?', NULL, 'policy', 'open_for_team', 'false', 'Checkout is not built. The billing screen waits two seconds and shows success, so any answer about how a payment behaves would be a promise we cannot keep. Writeable the day Razorpay is wired. The answer also differs by plan now: Starter is a one-off payment and must never set up a recurring charge, while Plus and Pro renew monthly. That distinction has to be true in the payment flow before it can be described here.', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'group-15-paying-invoices-cancelling.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('181', '15', 'paying-invoices-cancelling', 'Paying, invoices, cancelling', 'How do I cancel?', NULL, 'policy', 'open_for_team', 'false', 'Checkout is not built. The billing screen waits two seconds and shows success, so any answer about how a payment behaves would be a promise we cannot keep. Writeable the day Razorpay is wired. There is no cancel path in the product and no decision on whether cancelling is self-serve or a support request.', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'group-15-paying-invoices-cancelling.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('182', '15', 'paying-invoices-cancelling', 'Paying, invoices, cancelling', 'Is GST included in the price?', 'Yes. Every price you see already includes GST.

Rs 199 for Starter, Rs 450 for Plus, Rs 999 for Pro and Rs 300 for a discovery call are all final figures. Nothing is added at checkout, so the number on the plans page is the number that leaves your account.

If you need a GST invoice for your business, ask us at info@goxl.in and we will sort it out.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-06', 'Team decision 2026-09-06: GST is included in all plan prices. Prices are inclusive, not exclusive.', NULL, 'Team decision, 2026-09-06.', 'group-15-paying-invoices-cancelling.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('183', '15', 'paying-invoices-cancelling', 'Paying, invoices, cancelling', 'Can I get a GST invoice in my company''s name?', NULL, 'policy', 'open_for_team', 'false', 'Not decided. GST is confirmed as included in the price, but whether we issue a GST invoice in a company''s name -- and how a founder supplies their GSTIN -- has not been settled, and no invoicing exists in the product. Answer 182 currently points founders at support for this.', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'group-15-paying-invoices-cancelling.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('184', '15', 'paying-invoices-cancelling', 'Paying, invoices, cancelling', 'What can I pay with? Is UPI supported?', NULL, 'policy', 'open_for_team', 'false', 'Checkout is not built. The billing screen waits two seconds and shows success, so any answer about how a payment behaves would be a promise we cannot keep. Writeable the day Razorpay is wired. Which methods are enabled is a Razorpay configuration choice nobody has made yet.', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'group-15-paying-invoices-cancelling.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('185', '15', 'paying-invoices-cancelling', 'Paying, invoices, cancelling', 'Can I pay from outside India?', NULL, 'policy', 'retired', 'false', NULL, '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'RETIRED by team decision 2026-09-06: Ally is taking users in India only for now, so this is not a question to put in front of founders. Kept in the bank with its id so it is not re-added by accident, and excluded from the export. Revisit if the product ever opens beyond India.', 'group-15-paying-invoices-cancelling.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('186', '15', 'paying-invoices-cancelling', 'Paying, invoices, cancelling', 'Do you store my card details?', NULL, 'policy', 'open_for_team', 'false', 'Checkout is not built. The billing screen waits two seconds and shows success, so any answer about how a payment behaves would be a promise we cannot keep. Writeable the day Razorpay is wired. The true answer will be that the payment provider holds them and we do not, but that must not be stated before the integration exists and has been checked.', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'group-15-paying-invoices-cancelling.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('187', '15', 'paying-invoices-cancelling', 'Paying, invoices, cancelling', 'If I cancel, do I keep access until the end of the month?', NULL, 'policy', 'open_for_team', 'false', 'Checkout is not built. The billing screen waits two seconds and shows success, so any answer about how a payment behaves would be a promise we cannot keep. Writeable the day Razorpay is wired. Whether a cancelled plan lapses at period end or immediately is a product decision that has not been made, and there is no cancel path to check it against.', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'group-15-paying-invoices-cancelling.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('188', '15', 'paying-invoices-cancelling', 'Paying, invoices, cancelling', 'If I downgrade, what happens to my report and my data?', 'Nothing is deleted. Ever, for this reason.

Your report, your Founder DNA, your goals, your tasks and your past conversations all stay exactly where they are. Moving to a smaller plan changes what you can do next -- it never takes away what you already have.

What does change is access to some features. If you move down from Plus to Starter, for example, you keep your report but you stop being able to chat with Ally.

Move back up later and everything is where you left it.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing,/app/report}', '2026-09-06', 'Consistent with how the product already behaves: plan features gate new actions, and nothing in the codebase deletes founder data on a plan change. Verified there is no downgrade cleanup path anywhere.', NULL, NULL, 'group-15-paying-invoices-cancelling.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('189', '15', 'paying-invoices-cancelling', 'Paying, invoices, cancelling', 'Can I get a refund if the report wasn''t useful?', 'It depends which plan you are on, and we would rather be plain about it.

On Plus and Pro, yes -- within 7 days of your payment. Write to info@goxl.in and ask, and we will refund you. After 7 days we do not give refunds.

On Starter, at Rs 199, there is no refund. It is a one-off payment for the diagnosis and your report, and once the report is written the work is done.

If the report is wrong about your business -- not just unwelcome, but factually wrong -- tell us regardless of the plan or the timing. That is worth fixing.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-06', 'Team decision 2026-09-06: no refund on Starter; Plus and Pro refundable within 7 days of payment on request, none after.', 'The 7-day window needs a stored payment date to run from, and support needs to be able to see it. Nothing records one today because nothing takes a payment. Build it into the checkout work.', 'Team decision, 2026-09-06.', 'group-15-paying-invoices-cancelling.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('190', '15', 'paying-invoices-cancelling', 'Paying, invoices, cancelling', 'Can I pause my subscription instead of cancelling?', NULL, 'policy', 'open_for_team', 'false', 'Not decided, and there is no subscription machinery to pause. Follows the cancel decision in 181 and 187.', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'group-15-paying-invoices-cancelling.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('191', '15', 'paying-invoices-cancelling', 'Paying, invoices, cancelling', 'I upgraded but the feature is still locked.', NULL, 'policy', 'open_for_team', 'false', 'Checkout is not built. The billing screen waits two seconds and shows success, so any answer about how a payment behaves would be a promise we cannot keep. Writeable the day Razorpay is wired. Nobody can upgrade yet, so this failure cannot happen or be reproduced.', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'group-15-paying-invoices-cancelling.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('192', '15', 'paying-invoices-cancelling', 'Paying, invoices, cancelling', 'Money left my account and nothing happened.', NULL, 'policy', 'open_for_team', 'false', 'Checkout is not built. The billing screen waits two seconds and shows success, so any answer about how a payment behaves would be a promise we cannot keep. Writeable the day Razorpay is wired. This is the most important answer in the group and the one least safe to guess at. It needs the real payment and reconciliation flow before a word of it is written.', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'group-15-paying-invoices-cancelling.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('193', '15', 'paying-invoices-cancelling', 'Paying, invoices, cancelling', 'Can I switch plans mid-month? Do I pay the difference?', NULL, 'policy', 'open_for_team', 'false', 'Checkout is not built. The billing screen waits two seconds and shows success, so any answer about how a payment behaves would be a promise we cannot keep. Writeable the day Razorpay is wired. Proration is a billing decision nobody has made, and Starter being a one-off rather than a subscription complicates it.', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'group-15-paying-invoices-cancelling.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('194', '15', 'paying-invoices-cancelling', 'Paying, invoices, cancelling', 'These are introductory prices. What happens when they go up?', NULL, 'policy', 'open_for_team', 'false', 'Not decided. Whether early founders keep their price, and for how long, is a commercial commitment the team has to make deliberately -- it is the kind of promise that is very hard to walk back once a support answer has made it.', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'group-15-paying-invoices-cancelling.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('195', '16', 'account-and-access', 'Account and access', 'How do I change my profile photo?', 'Go to Profile and click your picture, then choose a new one.

It accepts PNG, JPEG and WEBP, up to 5MB. The new photo replaces the old one straight away -- there is nothing to save.

One thing that catches people out: iPhones save photos as HEIC by default, and that is not accepted yet. If your photo will not upload, that is almost always why. Open it and export it as JPEG, or change Settings, then Camera, then Formats to "Most Compatible" so new photos are saved as JPEG.

If it still will not go, tell us what kind of file it is.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Live test: PNG upload returned 201 with a stored avatar URL; a GIF was refused with a clear message naming the accepted types. One photo per founder -- a new upload replaces the old.', NULL, 'Same HEIC gap recorded against question 219. The picker''s accept list means iPhone photos are greyed out in the file chooser with no error to read.', 'group-16-account-and-access.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('196', '16', 'account-and-access', 'Account and access', 'Can I change the email on my account?', 'Not yourself, but we can do it. Write to info@goxl.in.

Tell us the address you have now and the one you want, and send it from an address we can recognise.

We do it by hand on purpose. Your email is what proves the account is yours, so it is not something a form should change quietly.

If you have only just signed up and have not done anything yet, the simpler route is to sign up again with the right address and tell us to remove the first one.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Live-checked: /settings/account accepts preferred_language and nothing else, and the schema states plainly that email and plan are owned by auth and billing rather than editable here.', 'There is no in-product way to even ASK for this. A founder who mistyped their address at signup is signed in as an address they do not own and cannot reach us from inside the account. Worth an ''email change'' action in the Privacy Center beside the correction request that already exists.', NULL, 'group-16-account-and-access.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('197', '16', 'account-and-access', 'Account and access', 'I can''t log in. I''ve forgotten my password.', 'You do not need it. Ask for a code instead.

On the sign-in screen, choose the option to sign in with a code, type your email address and we send you an 8-digit code. Enter it and you can set a new password there and then.

The code takes a moment to arrive and it is often in spam. If nothing comes, wait 60 seconds and press Resend.

If your email address is the problem -- you cannot get into that inbox any more -- write to info@goxl.in and we will help.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/guided/login}', '2026-09-05', 'Walked the sign-in flow: the email-and-code path is both the first sign-in and the forgotten-password route, and it ends by setting a new password. Codes are 8 digits and Resend unlocks after 60 seconds.', NULL, NULL, 'group-16-account-and-access.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('198', '16', 'account-and-access', 'Account and access', 'Can I use the same account on my phone and my laptop?', 'Yes. Sign in on both and use whichever suits you.

Everything is stored on our side, not on the device, so your report, your goals and your conversations are the same wherever you open them. Something you write on your phone is there on your laptop.

Signing in on one does not sign you out of the other.

The only thing worth knowing is that long documents -- your report especially -- are easier to read on a bigger screen.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app}', '2026-09-05', 'Sessions are per browser: each device gets its own refresh token and signing in on one does not disturb another. All state is server-side.', NULL, NULL, 'group-16-account-and-access.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('199', '16', 'account-and-access', 'Account and access', 'I share a laptop. How do I sign out everywhere?', 'There is no button for that yet, and I would rather tell you than let you look for one.

Signing out only signs out the device you are on.

So on a shared laptop, the thing that matters is signing out on that laptop when you finish -- use Sign out in Profile rather than just closing the tab. That does end the session on that machine properly.

If you think someone else has been in your account, write to info@goxl.in and say so. We will help you secure it, and we would want to know.

We are looking at adding a proper "sign out everywhere".', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile,/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Confirmed in code: /auth/logout revokes only the single refresh token presented, and revoked_tokens is keyed by jti with no founder_id column -- so no query exists that could end every session for one founder.', 'Cannot be built without a schema change, and it is the security control founders actually ask for. Needs a founder_id on revoked_tokens or a per-founder token generation counter. This is the control worth having instead of the session_timeout_minutes setting removed on 2026-09-05 -- it closes a real hole rather than a decorative one.', NULL, 'group-16-account-and-access.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('200', '16', 'account-and-access', 'Account and access', 'I run two businesses. Can I have both on one account?', 'No, one account is one business.

Running two means two accounts with two email addresses, and paying for each.

That is deliberate rather than a limitation we have not got to. Everything Ally builds -- your stage, your report, your goals -- is about one business. Two businesses in one account would give you a blurred read of both.

If you do run both accounts, use whichever fits the business you are working on that day. They stay completely separate.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-06', 'Team decision 2026-09-06: multi-business accounts are not available. Confirmed in the product: one profile, one diagnosis, one report per account.', NULL, 'Team decision, 2026-09-06.', 'group-16-account-and-access.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('201', '16', 'account-and-access', 'Account and access', 'Can I give my cofounder access?', 'No, there is no way to add a second person to your account.

No invite, no extra seat, no shared login. And please do not share your password -- everything in your account is tied to that one sign-in, including your billing.

If your cofounder wants their own read, they can sign up separately. Their diagnosis would be about them, which is the point -- Ally is looking at the founder as much as the business, and the two of you will not answer the same way.

Comparing the two reports is usually more useful than sharing one.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-06', 'Team decision 2026-09-06: cofounder access is not available. Confirmed in the product: no second seat, no invite mechanism and no shared account exist.', NULL, 'Team decision, 2026-09-06.', 'group-16-account-and-access.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('202', '16', 'account-and-access', 'Account and access', 'Is there a mobile app?', 'No app yet, but Ally works in your phone''s browser.

Just open the site on your phone and sign in as usual. The menu moves to a button in the top left, and the pages fit the smaller screen.

Long things like your report are easier to read on a laptop, so if you have one, use it for the report and your phone for quick check-ins.

We do not have an app in the app stores yet.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app}', '2026-09-05', 'Tested at 375x812: the main pages render with no horizontal overflow and the sidebar collapses to a menu button. There is no PWA manifest and no app store presence.', NULL, NULL, 'group-16-account-and-access.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('203', '16', 'account-and-access', 'Account and access', 'Which browsers does this work on?', 'Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari, as long as they are reasonably up to date.

Anything from the last two or three years is fine, on a computer or a phone. Internet Explorer is not supported at all.

If a page looks broken or will not load, the two things worth trying are updating your browser and doing a hard refresh, which clears the old copy your browser is holding.

If it still misbehaves, tell us which browser and version you are on. That is usually enough for us to find it.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'React 19 on Vite 8, built for baseline-widely-available browsers. No legacy build and no polyfill bundle ships, so genuinely old browsers will not run the app at all.', NULL, NULL, 'group-16-account-and-access.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('204', '17', 'privacy-data-and-trust', 'Privacy, data and trust', 'Can you read my conversations?', 'Yes, a small number of people at GoXL can, and we would rather say that plainly than let you assume otherwise.

It is limited, and it is for support. If you write in saying Ally gave you a strange answer, somebody has to be able to look at what actually happened.

They can read. They cannot edit — there is no way for anyone here to change what you or Ally said, because that was never built.

Your conversations are not shared outside GoXL, not sold, and never shown to other founders.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Support and above hold VIEW_CHATS. The admin service has no write counterpart anywhere — deliberately, so ''view but never edit'' is guaranteed by absence rather than by a guard.', NULL, NULL, 'group-17-privacy-data-and-trust.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('205', '17', 'privacy-data-and-trust', 'Privacy, data and trust', 'Who else sees my diagnosis?', 'Nobody outside GoXL.

Inside GoXL, a small number of people can open it for support reasons — the same people who can look at a conversation if you report a problem.

It is not shared with other founders, not sold, and not shown to investors or partners. There is no directory, no ranking, and no way for another founder to find you.

If you do want somebody to see it, that is your call: your report has a Share button that creates a link, and you decide who gets it.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/report}', '2026-09-05', 'Reports are readable by admins holding VIEW_REPORTS. No cross-founder visibility exists anywhere in the product. Sharing is founder-initiated and revocable.', NULL, NULL, 'group-17-privacy-data-and-trust.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('206', '17', 'privacy-data-and-trust', 'Privacy, data and trust', 'Is my data used to train anything?', 'Your own writing, never. Anonymous combined data, yes.

Here is the line, because it matters. Your answers, your report and your conversations are not used to train any AI model. They are not put into any searchable index either. They are stored as your records and read back for you, and nothing else.

What we may use is anonymous, combined information -- patterns across many founders, with nothing in them that could be traced back to you or your business. That is how Ally gets better at reading the next founder.

Our Terms and Privacy Policy both say this in full, and they are the authority if you want the exact wording.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/privacy,/terms}', '2026-09-05', 'Settled by the team on 2026-09-05: the position is what the Terms and Privacy Policy already say. Terms section 4, Privacy Policy sections 3(c) and 6 all permit anonymised aggregated use to improve GoXL''s AI models. The first half is separately verified in code -- the eight embedded tables are all GoXL reference knowledge, and no founder-owned table carries an embedding column, so founder text is never vectorised or trained on.', NULL, 'Team decision, 2026-09-05. Earlier drafts of this answer said flatly that nothing is used to train any model, which contradicted three clauses in our own published documents. The team''s call was to follow the documents. The distinction the answer draws -- your writing never, anonymous aggregate yes -- is exactly the distinction the Terms draw, and it is the honest one.', 'group-17-privacy-data-and-trust.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('207', '17', 'privacy-data-and-trust', 'Privacy, data and trust', 'How do I delete everything?', 'Go to Profile, then Privacy Center, then "Delete my account".

That schedules erasure with a 30-day window. Until that date your account works normally and nothing has been removed, so a mis-click is recoverable.

If you change your mind, just sign in again before the date and we will offer you the chance to cancel it.

If you want a copy of your data before it goes, use "Download my data" on the same page first. After the date, it cannot be recovered.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Deletion is scheduled with a 30-day grace window. Signing in during it shows a blocking prompt offering a one-click cancel.', NULL, NULL, 'group-17-privacy-data-and-trust.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('208', '17', 'privacy-data-and-trust', 'Privacy, data and trust', 'Where is my data stored? Is it in India?', 'Yes. Your data is stored in India — our servers and database run in the Mumbai region.

That is a deliberate choice for a product built for Indian founders: your business information stays in the country rather than being moved somewhere else for convenience.

If you need the specifics for a compliance or diligence question, write to support and we will give you a proper answer rather than a summary.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'The application load balancer and the Supabase project are both in ap-south-1 (Mumbai).', 'CONFIRM BEFORE PUBLISHING. Production runs on AWS RDS, and its region has not been verified from here — only the load balancer and the Supabase project were. A data residency claim is one of the few things worth being certain about. See docs/PRODUCTION-RDS-CHECKS.md.', NULL, 'group-17-privacy-data-and-trust.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('209', '17', 'privacy-data-and-trust', 'Privacy, data and trust', 'Does what I type go to an outside AI company?', 'Yes, in a limited and anonymous way, and our privacy policy says so.

Ally uses outside AI services to do some of its thinking. What goes to them is anonymised first, and they are bound by data handling agreements that stop them keeping it or using it for their own purposes.

What does not happen: your name, your business name and your account are not part of what is sent, and nothing you write is used to train anyone''s model.

We do not name which services we use. That is a commercial decision and it can change.

If you need the specifics for a compliance review, write to us and we will answer properly.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/privacy,/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Privacy Policy section 5(b), verbatim: ''AI Processing Services -- anonymised diagnostic data may be processed by third-party LLM providers under strict data handling agreements.'' That discloses the category without naming a vendor, which is exactly what the never-name-the-model rule needs.', NULL, 'Was open_for_team. Unblocked by reading the published Privacy Policy, which had already answered it at the right level of detail -- the collision with ''never name the model'' was only ever a collision if we tried to answer it more specifically than the policy does.', 'group-17-privacy-data-and-trust.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('210', '17', 'privacy-data-and-trust', 'Privacy, data and trust', 'Can someone at GoXL open my account and read it?', 'Yes, and we would rather you knew than found out.

A small number of people here can open your account to help with a problem — your profile, your report, your conversations. It is limited to the people who answer founders.

They can look. They cannot change anything you or Ally wrote; that was never built.

Anything they do change — resetting something, correcting a record — is written to a log with who did it and when.

Nobody outside GoXL has this access, and none of it is shared or sold.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Read capabilities are VIEW_USERS, VIEW_REPORTS and VIEW_CHATS. Every mutation records an audit entry with admin, founder, action and IP. No edit path exists for founder or Ally messages.', NULL, NULL, 'group-17-privacy-data-and-trust.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('211', '17', 'privacy-data-and-trust', 'Privacy, data and trust', 'What does "pause AI processing" do, and what stops working if I use it?', 'It stops Ally thinking about you, and nothing else.

While it is on you cannot send messages to Ally or start a diagnosis. Both stop with a notice telling you to resume from the Privacy Center.

Everything you already have stays exactly as it is. Your account is active, your report is readable, and nothing is deleted.

You can turn it back on whenever you like — there is a Resume button in the amber banner at the top of Profile, then Privacy Center, and it takes effect straight away.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Tested live: with processing restricted, a chat message returns a clear refusal naming the Privacy Center. Nothing stored is affected, and resuming restores normal function immediately.', NULL, NULL, 'group-17-privacy-data-and-trust.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('212', '17', 'privacy-data-and-trust', 'Privacy, data and trust', 'What''s actually in the data export? Can I read it?', 'Everything we hold about you, as a file that downloads straight away.

It covers 23 areas: your profile and settings, your diagnosis sessions and answers, your Founder DNA answers, your reports, your conversations and messages, your goals and tasks, calls you booked, feedback you sent, and the record of privacy requests like this one.

It is a JSON file. That is readable rather than pretty — open it in a browser or any text editor and you will find your way around.

If you need it in a different form, ask support.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile,/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Ran the export: 23 named sections, served immediately as JSON.', NULL, NULL, 'group-17-privacy-data-and-trust.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('213', '17', 'privacy-data-and-trust', 'Privacy, data and trust', 'If I delete my account, is it gone immediately?', 'No, and that is on purpose.

Deletion is scheduled with a 30-day window. Until that date your account works normally and nothing has been removed — so if you clicked it by mistake, or simply changed your mind, you have time.

Sign in again before the date and we will offer to cancel it. You do not have to email anybody.

After the date it is permanent and cannot be undone, so take a copy of anything you want to keep before then.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', '30-day grace window with a self-serve cancel offered on next sign-in.', NULL, NULL, 'group-17-privacy-data-and-trust.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('214', '17', 'privacy-data-and-trust', 'Privacy, data and trust', 'Can I use Ally without giving my real business name?', 'Yes. Your business name is optional and nothing is blocked without it.

Ally works from what you describe — your stage, who you serve, what is stuck — rather than from who you are. Leave the name out or keep it vague and the diagnosis is unaffected.

What does matter is being honest about the situation itself. A made-up business name costs you nothing. A made-up answer about your revenue costs you the accuracy of the report.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/guided/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'business_name is an optional column and nothing in the profile or diagnosis path requires it.', NULL, NULL, 'group-17-privacy-data-and-trust.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('215', '17', 'privacy-data-and-trust', 'Privacy, data and trust', 'Could anything I say here ever be shown to an investor or a partner?', 'Not by us. Never.

We do not share your data with investors, partners or anyone else outside GoXL, and we do not sell it.

The only way anything of yours reaches someone else is if you send it. Your report has a Share button that creates a link, and you decide who gets it.

If you would rather nothing was shareable at all, simply do not create one.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/report}', '2026-09-05', 'The only outbound path for founder content is a founder-created share link, which is revocable and expires after 30 days.', NULL, NULL, 'group-17-privacy-data-and-trust.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('216', '17', 'privacy-data-and-trust', 'Privacy, data and trust', 'If I stop using it, do you keep my data forever?', 'We keep it until you ask us to delete it. There is no automatic clear-out after a stretch of not using Ally.

That is deliberate: you can come back in a year and your report is still there, rather than having quietly disappeared while you were busy.

If you would rather it did not sit there, you can delete your account whenever you like from Profile, then Privacy Center — with the same 30-day window before it becomes permanent.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'No inactivity-based retention or purge job exists anywhere. The only deletion path is founder-initiated.', NULL, NULL, 'group-17-privacy-data-and-trust.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('217', '18', 'when-something-breaks', 'When something breaks', 'I uploaded a file and Ally says it can''t see it.', 'Ally can read documents. It cannot read pictures.

PDFs, Word files, plain text and CSV all work. Ally reads what is inside them and can quote your own numbers back to you.

Images are different. A PNG, a JPEG or a screenshot will upload, but Ally cannot see what is in it. The same is true of a photo or a scan of a document.

If your file is a picture, the quickest fix is to type the important part into the chat, or upload the original document instead of a photo of it.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/ally-chat}', '2026-09-05', 'Uploaded a CSV and Ally quoted the exact figures back. Uploaded a PNG and it correctly said it could not read the contents -- it no longer claims to have looked at it.', NULL, 'Ally used to claim it had read images it could never see. The prompt said ''attached for you to look at'' while the transport carried text only. Fixed on 2026-09-04 by setting the media limit to zero, so the model is never told an image is there.', 'group-18-when-something-breaks.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('218', '18', 'when-something-breaks', 'When something breaks', 'My calendar won''t connect.', 'Go to Plan Your Day and press Connect calendar. Google asks you to sign in and allow access. When you come back, the page tells you what happened.

If it did not work, the message on that page says why. The three common ones:

"Link expired" means you took too long on the Google screen. Press Connect again.

"Google refused the connection" often means you signed in with a different Google account. Use the one your calendar is on.

If you pressed Cancel on the Google screen, nothing was saved. Just start again.

If it keeps failing, write to us and tell us which message you saw.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/plan}', '2026-09-05', 'Read the callback: it always redirects back to Plan Your Day carrying one of four outcomes, each with a readable sentence. Calendar sync is confirmed working on production by the founder who owns that account.', NULL, NULL, 'group-18-when-something-breaks.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('219', '18', 'when-something-breaks', 'When something breaks', 'My profile photo won''t upload.', 'Ally accepts PNG, JPEG and WEBP, up to 5MB.

The most common reason it fails is an iPhone photo. iPhones save pictures as HEIC by default, and that is not accepted yet. GIFs are not accepted either.

The fix is to open the photo and save or export it as JPEG, then upload that.

On an iPhone you can also change Settings, then Camera, then Formats to "Most Compatible", so new photos are saved as JPEG from then on.

If the file is very large, make it smaller first.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Live test: PNG returned 201 with a stored avatar URL. A GIF was refused with a clear message naming the accepted types. HEIC is neither accepted server-side nor offered in the picker.', 'On an iPhone the founder''s own photos are greyed out in the file chooser, so there is no error to read and nothing to explain the failure. Accept HEIC and convert, or add one line of help text beside the button.', NULL, 'group-18-when-something-breaks.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('220', '18', 'when-something-breaks', 'When something breaks', 'The page is stuck on "thinking".', 'That screen is waiting for your report to be built. It usually takes under a minute.

If it is taking longer, the screen says so and tells you that you can close it. That is true. Your answers are all saved, and leaving the page loses nothing.

Come back to Report from the menu a few minutes later and it will be there.

If it is still not there an hour later, write to us and tell us roughly when you finished. We will find it.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/report}', '2026-09-05', 'The screen polls for the report every 4 seconds and switches its own copy to ''This is taking longer than usual. Your answers are saved.'' after about two minutes. It never spins silently.', NULL, NULL, 'group-18-when-something-breaks.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('221', '18', 'when-something-breaks', 'When something breaks', 'I found a bug. Where do I report it?', 'Go to Help & Support and press "Report a bug". That opens the Feedback page with the right topic already chosen, so you only have to describe what happened.

The most useful thing you can tell us is what you were doing just before it broke, and what you saw on screen. A screenshot helps more than anything.

It comes straight to our team. It is not a form that goes nowhere.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help,/app/feedback}', '2026-09-05', 'The Help & Support quick action carries the topic through to the Feedback page, and the note posts to the backend and lands in founder_feedback.', NULL, NULL, 'group-18-when-something-breaks.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('222', '18', 'when-something-breaks', 'When something breaks', 'My report page is blank.', 'There are two different things this can be.

If you have not finished a diagnosis yet, the page says "Your report isn''t ready yet" and offers a button to start one. That is the normal state, not a fault.

If you have done the diagnosis and the page is empty, it is almost always still loading. Give it a moment, then refresh the page.

If a refresh does not fix it, write to us. Your report is stored on our side, so a blank page never means it has been lost.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/report}', '2026-09-05', 'Opened /app/report on an account with no diagnosis: a proper empty state with a Start Founder Diagnosis button. The only genuinely blank moment is the second or two while it loads.', NULL, NULL, 'group-18-when-something-breaks.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('223', '18', 'when-something-breaks', 'When something breaks', 'It signed me out in the middle of the diagnosis.', 'Sign back in and carry on. You will not have to start again.

Every answer is saved the moment you send it, so the diagnosis picks up from the question you were on.

It also does not count as a used diagnosis. Only a finished one counts, so nothing has been spent.

Being signed out part way through is unusual. It normally means you signed out somewhere else, or your browser cleared its stored data. If it keeps happening, tell us which browser you use and we will look.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/diagnosis}', '2026-09-05', 'Answers are persisted one at a time on submit, and the submit path is idempotent when resumed. Sessions renew automatically for 30 days, so a mid-session sign-out is genuinely rare.', NULL, NULL, 'group-18-when-something-breaks.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('224', '18', 'when-something-breaks', 'When something breaks', 'It says I''ve hit a limit and I''ve only just started.', 'The daily allowance is not counted in messages. It is counted in words, roughly speaking, and a long message costs a lot more than a short one.

Ally also reads your report and your profile before it replies, so even a short question is not free.

That is why a handful of long messages can use up a day, and it is not a fault.

The message you saw says which limit you reached, and your billing page shows today''s usage against your allowance.

If that page shows you have barely used anything and you are still blocked, that is a fault. Write to us.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/billing}', '2026-09-05', 'Measured the real cost from the database: 54 messages, average 1,305 tokens, largest 2,776. The daily error names the exact numbers and the reset time, so a founder can check it against the billing page.', 'On Plus (Rs 450, 3,500 tokens a day) that average works out at two or three messages. This complaint will be literally true for a founder who has just paid, on their first sitting. The ceiling needs raising -- no support answer covers it.', NULL, 'group-18-when-something-breaks.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('225', '18', 'when-something-breaks', 'When something breaks', 'Everything is very slow.', 'Two things are usually behind it.

The first is the Compass page. It gathers a lot at once and is the slowest page in Ally, especially the first time you open it after signing in. We know, and we are working on it.

The second is simply a slow connection. Ally sends a fair amount back and forth.

If one particular page is slow every single time, tell us which one and roughly how long it takes. That is far more useful to us than "it is slow", and it gets fixed faster.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app}', '2026-09-05', 'Compass took several seconds to fill in on a warm local build with no other load. Traced earlier to database pool contention when its panels all load together.', NULL, NULL, 'group-18-when-something-breaks.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('226', '18', 'when-something-breaks', 'When something breaks', 'It looks broken on my phone.', 'Ally works in a phone browser. We checked the main pages at phone size and they fit, with nothing running off the side of the screen.

There is no app to install yet. Use Chrome or Safari.

If a page looks wrong, it is usually an old copy stored by your browser after we released an update. Pull down to refresh, or close the tab and open it again.

If it still looks wrong, send us a screenshot and tell us which phone you have. That is the only way we can see what you are seeing.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Tested at 375x812: /app, /app/report and /app/ally-chat all render with zero horizontal overflow and the sidebar collapses to a menu button.', NULL, NULL, 'group-18-when-something-breaks.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('227', '18', 'when-something-breaks', 'When something breaks', 'Where does my feedback actually go? Does anyone read it?', 'It comes to our team, and yes, we read all of it.

Both things on the Feedback page, the written note and the star rating, are saved on our side and show up for the team straight away.

This used to be worse. The written note used to open your own email app, which quietly did nothing if you did not have one set up. That is fixed. It now reaches us directly.

We do not reply to every one. If you would like an answer, say so in the note.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/feedback}', '2026-09-05', 'Both the note and the rating POST to the same endpoint and land in the same founder_feedback table, which the team reads.', NULL, NULL, 'group-18-when-something-breaks.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('228', '18', 'when-something-breaks', 'When something breaks', 'If I message support, how long until someone replies?', 'We aim to reply within one working day.

We are here Monday to Friday, 9 AM to 6 PM India time. A message sent on Saturday evening will be picked up on Monday.

You can reach us at info@goxl.in, or through Help & Support inside Ally, which sends your name and email along so you do not have to repeat them.

If it is urgent, say so at the top of your message. Money leaving your account, or not being able to get in, go to the front of the queue.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Read from the Help & Support page as it stands today: info@goxl.in, Mon-Fri 9 AM - 6 PM IST, ''We aim to reply within one working day.'' Stated as an aim, with no invented average.', NULL, NULL, 'group-18-when-something-breaks.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('229', '19', 'what-ally-actually-is', 'What Ally actually is', 'Is Ally a coach, a consultant, or a tool?', 'None of the three, and the difference matters.

A coach asks you questions. A consultant hands you answers. A tool waits for you to know what to do with it.

Ally is a compass. It works out where you actually are first -- you and the business -- and then points at the one thing to move next.

The way we put it is this: most AI gives you answers, Ally helps you find the right question. The problem you can see is often not the problem you need to solve.

So it is not there to advise you, or to be clever. It is there so you stop guessing which problem is the real one.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'The settled position, matching the landing page word for word: ''Your Founder''s Compass'' and ''Most AI gives you answers. Ally helps you find the right question.''', NULL, NULL, 'group-19-what-ally-actually-is.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('230', '19', 'what-ally-actually-is', 'What Ally actually is', 'Can this replace a real mentor or advisor?', 'No, and we would not want it to.

A good mentor gives you judgement, a network, and someone who has done it before and cares how it goes for you. Ally has none of that.

What Ally has is different. It is there at eleven at night. It has read every answer you gave it. It never gets tired of the same question, and it has no reason to tell you what you want to hear.

The useful way to use both is together. Bring your report to your mentor. It saves the first hour of every conversation.

If you want a person from our side, you can book a discovery call.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/discovery-call}', '2026-09-05', 'Consistent with answers 76 and 147: a discovery call is 30 minutes with a real person, and the report is what makes that conversation start somewhere useful.', NULL, NULL, 'group-19-what-ally-actually-is.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('231', '19', 'what-ally-actually-is', 'What Ally actually is', 'Is a human involved in any of what I get?', 'In your report, no. It was written by AI, and no person read it before you did.

People built what it works from. The framework, the questions, the six areas and the way a root cause is found were all designed by our team. Ally cannot go outside that, and it is not allowed to invent findings.

There are two places a person is genuinely involved. A discovery call is 30 minutes with someone from our team. And when you message support, a person replies.

We would rather be plain about this than let you imagine somebody is reading over your shoulder.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/report,/app/discovery-call}', '2026-09-05', 'Matches answer 44. The report is generated with no human review step anywhere in the pipeline. The prompt forbids inventing findings. Discovery calls and support are the two human surfaces.', NULL, NULL, 'group-19-what-ally-actually-is.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('232', '19', 'what-ally-actually-is', 'What Ally actually is', 'Who built this, and what qualifies them to diagnose my business?', 'GoXL built it. Entrepreneurs, building for entrepreneurs.

But the honest answer to "what qualifies it" is not somebody''s CV. It is what sits underneath.

Ally was built from real founder work: more than 10,000 founder case studies, and 25,000 founder problems traced back to what actually caused them, across more than a hundred areas.

And the root cause is not an AI''s opinion. Your answers are scored against that framework, and the framework decides. The AI''s job is to explain the result in plain language, not to reach it.

If you want to talk to the people behind it, book a discovery call.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/discovery-call}', '2026-09-05', 'Corpus figures are the landing page''s own, verbatim, and match answers 34 and 60. ''For the entrepreneurs, by the entrepreneurs'' is the landing page''s phrase. The deterministic-engine point is true of the code: the engine picks the root cause and the model narrates it.', 'Nothing public names the team or their track record. If a founder pushes past this answer we have nothing to give them. A short ''about us'' page the bot can point at would close it.', NULL, 'group-19-what-ally-actually-is.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('233', '19', 'what-ally-actually-is', 'What Ally actually is', 'Do you work with my competitors?', 'Possibly. Anyone can sign up, and we do not offer exclusivity to anyone in any industry.

What matters is that it changes nothing for you. Nothing of yours is ever visible to another founder. There is no directory, no ranking, and no way for anyone to find you or to see your report.

You are not compared against named businesses either. Your report measures you against the framework, not against the founder down the road.

Your data is never sold, and never shared outside GoXL.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'No exclusivity mechanism exists anywhere in the product, and no cross-founder visibility of any kind. Consistent with answers 38 and 205.', NULL, NULL, 'group-19-what-ally-actually-is.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('234', '19', 'what-ally-actually-is', 'What Ally actually is', 'Is this only for Indian founders?', 'It is built for Indian founders, but it is not closed to anyone else.

Almost everything is set up around India. Prices are in rupees. Your data is stored in India. Support runs Monday to Friday, 9 AM to 6 PM India time.

Nothing in Ally checks where you are, so it works wherever you sit. The questions are about your stage and your business, not your country.

If you are outside India and thinking of paying, write to us first. We would rather sort that out with you than have you find a problem at checkout.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'No geographic restriction exists in the code. Prices are in INR, support hours are IST, and residency is India. Deliberately does not promise foreign payment -- question 185 is still open.', NULL, 'Kept vague on paying from outside India on purpose. Question 185 (foreign payment) is still with the team, and checkout is not built.', 'group-19-what-ally-actually-is.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('235', '19', 'what-ally-actually-is', 'What Ally actually is', 'Is my business too small -- or too big -- for this?', 'Almost certainly not.

There are eight stages, from just exploring an idea all the way to exit. You do not need revenue, customers, a team, or even a registered company. If you only have an idea, Ideation is a real stage and the diagnosis is built for it.

At the other end, Ally is built around a founder-led business -- one person whose decisions still shape the company. If you have a full leadership team and your own decisions are no longer the constraint, less of it will apply.

Solo founders, small teams, family businesses and bootstrapped builders are all squarely who this is for.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/guided/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'founder_stages holds all eight stages from Ideation to Exit, and the diagnosis scopes itself to fewer pillars at the early ones rather than refusing them. The audience list is the landing page''s own.', NULL, NULL, 'group-19-what-ally-actually-is.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('236', '19', 'what-ally-actually-is', 'What Ally actually is', 'What''s coming next? Can I ask for a feature?', 'Yes, please do. Go to Feedback and choose "I have an idea". It comes straight to our team, and we read all of it.

We do not publish a roadmap, mainly because we would rather not promise dates we then miss.

One thing we have committed to in writing: being able to run the diagnosis again when your business stage changes. That is intended, and not built yet.

If you tell us what you want and why, it genuinely counts. Several things in Ally are there because a founder asked.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/feedback}', '2026-09-05', 'The Feedback page''s ''I have an idea'' topic posts to founder_feedback, which the team reads. The re-run commitment is the only forward promise made anywhere in the answer set (answer 85), so it is the only one repeated here.', NULL, NULL, 'group-19-what-ally-actually-is.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('237', '19', 'what-ally-actually-is', 'What Ally actually is', 'What does Ally deliberately not do?', 'A short and honest list.

It does not invent things about your business. It works only from what you told it and what the framework found.

It does not answer questions about the product itself -- your plan, your bill, your allowance. That is what Help & Support is for.

It does not produce files. It will help you write a pitch deck in the chat, but it cannot hand you a PowerPoint. Your report is the one document you can download.

It does not chase you. No emails, no nudges outside the app.

It does not rank you against other founders, and it never shows your work to anyone else.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Every item on this list is a real, checked behaviour: the no-invention rule is in the system prompt, the help-content boundary is answer 99, the no-file-export limit is answer 91, the no-outbound-nudge limit is answer 137, and no cross-founder visibility exists anywhere.', 'Legal, tax and investment advice was deliberately LEFT OFF this list. No such boundary exists in the product -- the prompt library, the knowledge base and the grounding prompts state nothing about what Ally may advise on. Question 100 is open for exactly this reason. Add it here only after the boundary is built, never before.', NULL, 'group-19-what-ally-actually-is.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('238', '20', 'what-the-website-promised', 'What the website promised', 'The site says 100+ dimensions. My report covers six areas. Which is it?', 'Both are true, and it is a fair thing to ask.

The six areas are how your findings are laid out so the report can be read: Founder Readiness, Market Clarity, Revenue Maturity, Product & Execution, Team & Leadership, and Strategic Clarity.

Underneath them sit more than a hundred smaller things Ally can look at. Founder DNA alone covers 15. Business DNA has its own set, and which ones apply depends on your stage.

So the six are the shelves, not the contents. If everything assessed was printed one by one, the report would be a spreadsheet, and you would not read it.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/report}', '2026-09-05', 'The ''100+ entrepreneurial dimensions'' claim is still on the live page and matches what the product does. Founder DNA''s 15 dimensions are in the enum; the six pillars are the report''s organising structure.', NULL, NULL, 'group-20-what-the-website-promised.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('239', '20', 'what-the-website-promised', 'What the website promised', 'Where is the founder health score the homepage promised me?', 'Your Compass page has it. It is called Founder Clarity, and it is a word rather than a number.

Business health sits next to it, in the same style.

If yours is empty, there are two likely reasons. You may not have finished a diagnosis yet. Or you are at Ideation stage, where we deliberately do not publish a business health reading, because there is not yet enough business to measure honestly.

A made-up number would be worse than a blank. That gap is on purpose.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app}', '2026-09-05', 'The live page no longer promises a health score, so the premise is retired -- but the Compass genuinely shows Founder Clarity as a band, and ideation-stage reports deliberately publish no business health figure. Consistent with answer 40.', NULL, 'Premise gone from the current site. Kept and answered because founders who read the older page will still ask.', 'group-20-what-the-website-promised.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('240', '20', 'what-the-website-promised', 'What the website promised', 'The demo showed a diagnosis confidence figure. Where''s mine?', 'It is on your report, not in the chat.

Near the top you will see a line like "Ally''s finding - High confidence". There are three levels: High, Moderate and Early.

If it says Early, your report also opens with a short note about certainty, explaining that Ally did not get quite enough to be sure.

We show it as a word on purpose. A number invites you to argue with the number instead of reading the finding.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/report}', '2026-09-05', 'The current sample dashboard shows no confidence readout at all, so the premise is retired. Confidence genuinely appears on the report as a band -- verified by opening a real report. Consistent with answers 47 and 48.', NULL, NULL, 'group-20-what-the-website-promised.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('241', '20', 'what-the-website-promised', 'What the website promised', 'It said three priority actions. I got a different number.', 'Three is what the website shows as an example, not a promise.

Your report gives you what your diagnosis actually supports. For most founders that is two or three. It is never a long list.

That is deliberate. A list of ten things to fix is the same as no list, because you will do none of them.

If you got fewer than you expected, it usually means Ally found one thing sitting underneath the rest, and would rather you did that one properly.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/report,/app/recommendations}', '2026-09-05', '''Three things to focus on first'' is still on the live page, shown as an illustration alongside made-up examples. The real count comes from the diagnosis. Consistent with answer 129.', NULL, NULL, 'group-20-what-the-website-promised.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('242', '20', 'what-the-website-promised', 'What the website promised', 'What is the "Clarity Method"? Is it something you invented?', 'That is not a name we use any more, so if you saw it, it was an older version of the site.

What sits behind Ally is our own framework, built deliberately rather than borrowed. Six areas, more than a hundred things underneath them, and a set of rules that traces what you told us back to the one cause sitting underneath.

It came out of real founder work: more than 10,000 founder case studies, and 25,000 founder problems traced back to what caused them.

So: made by us, but not made up.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'The term ''Clarity Method'' appears nowhere on the live site. The framework description matches answer 34 and the landing page''s own corpus figures.', NULL, NULL, 'group-20-what-the-website-promised.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('243', '20', 'what-the-website-promised', 'What the website promised', 'The site calls it a Clarity Report. Inside it''s just "report". Same thing?', 'Same thing. One document, two names, and that is our untidiness rather than yours.

Inside Ally the page is called Report, and the browser tab still says "Clarity report". They are the same document, built from the same diagnosis.

There is only ever one report per account, so there is nothing to mix up. Whatever it is called, it is the one you are looking at.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/report}', '2026-09-05', 'Walked it: the app''s own page title is literally ''Clarity report - Ally - GoXL'' while the sidebar says Report. The term no longer appears on the live marketing site.', NULL, NULL, 'group-20-what-the-website-promised.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('244', '20', 'what-the-website-promised', 'What the website promised', 'Can I see a sample report before I sign up?', 'No, and we have decided not to make one.

There is a sample of the app on our website, so you can look around and see how it is laid out. But there is no sample report, and there will not be.

The reason is that a report only means anything with a real founder''s answers behind it. A made-up one would look impressive and tell you nothing about whether it would be useful to you -- and it would set an expectation your own report might not match, because yours is about your business, not a tidy invented one.

If you want a proper sense of it before deciding, ask support and we will talk you through what is in one.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Team decision 2026-09-05: no sample report will be produced. The site''s embedded sample dashboard (/ally-dashboard.html) remains and is what the answer points at.', NULL, 'Team decision, 2026-09-05.', 'group-20-what-the-website-promised.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('245', '20', 'what-the-website-promised', 'What the website promised', 'It says "no sales call". So what is the discovery call?', 'The current site does not make that claim, so it may have been an older version.

Either way, here is the plain answer. A discovery call is 30 minutes with someone from our team, and it costs Rs 300. It is not included free on any plan.

It is not a pitch. There is nothing to upsell you to on the call, because the plans are on the website and you can read them yourself.

The useful version is you bringing something specific: your report, a decision you are stuck on, or a finding you disagree with.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/discovery-call}', '2026-09-05', 'The phrase ''no sales call'' appears nowhere on the live site. Call price and shape match the team''s decision of 2026-09-05: Rs 300 per 30-minute call, on every plan.', NULL, 'Price set by the team on 2026-09-05. Raised from Rs 199 so it is not confused with the Rs 199 monthly Starter plan.', 'group-20-what-the-website-promised.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('246', '20', 'what-the-website-promised', 'What the website promised', 'It says private and encrypted. Encrypted how, and from whom?', 'Encrypted on the way to us, and encrypted where it is stored.

Everything between you and Ally travels over an encrypted connection, so nobody in between can read it. Where it is stored, it is encrypted there too. Connected accounts like your calendar have their keys encrypted separately, and if that encryption is not available the feature switches itself off rather than storing anything in the clear.

Now the part the word "encrypted" can hide.

Encrypted from outsiders, yes. Not from us. A small number of people at GoXL can open your account to help with a support problem. They can read. They cannot edit.

It is never sold, and never shown to other founders.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile,/privacy}', '2026-09-06', 'Verified in the repo: all traffic is HTTPS, and calendar tokens are encrypted with a key whose absence disables the feature rather than falling back to plaintext. Encryption at rest confirmed by the team on 2026-09-06 -- it is in place, matching the Privacy Policy section 8 claim of AES-256. Staff read access (VIEW_CHATS, VIEW_REPORTS) is real and has no write counterpart anywhere.', NULL, 'Team decision, 2026-09-06. The at-rest half was previously withheld because it could not be verified from the codebase while the Privacy Policy already claimed it publicly. The team has confirmed it is in place, so the answer now matches the policy.', 'group-20-what-the-website-promised.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('247', '20', 'what-the-website-promised', 'What the website promised', 'What should I have ready before I start?', 'Nothing you have to look up. That is rather the point.

It helps to have a rough sense of three things: what stage you are at, roughly how much money is coming in and from how many customers, and what is actually stuck right now.

You do not need documents, exact figures, or anything to upload. Ally asks in plain language, and approximate answers are fine.

What does matter is being honest rather than tidy. A polished answer gets you a polished report about a business that does not exist.

Set aside about half an hour, somewhere you can think.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/guided/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Walked the guided flow: nothing in onboarding or the diagnosis requires a document, an exact figure, or a registered company. Consistent with answers 13, 25 and 214.', NULL, NULL, 'group-20-what-the-website-promised.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('248', '20', 'what-the-website-promised', 'What the website promised', 'How long does the whole thing take, start to finish?', 'About 30 to 40 minutes, and you can stop whenever you like.

Setting up your profile takes under five minutes. Founder DNA is up to 16 questions. The diagnosis itself is between 14 and 32 questions, depending on your stage -- early-stage founders get fewer, because there is less business to ask about.

Then the report is built for you. That usually takes under a minute.

Nothing has to be done in one sitting. Every answer is saved as you send it, so you can close the tab and come back.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/guided/profile,/app/diagnosis}', '2026-09-05', 'Question budgets read from founder_stages: 14 at Ideation up to 32 at Expansion and Maturity. Founder DNA is capped at 16. The site''s own ''under 5 minutes'' onboarding and ''20 to 30 minutes, resumable'' diagnosis match this.', NULL, NULL, 'group-20-what-the-website-promised.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('249', '21', 'signing-in', 'Signing in', 'Why is there no password? I don''t want a code every time.', 'You do have a password, and you will not need a code every time.

The code is only for two moments: the very first time you sign in, and if you forget your password later.

When you enter that code, you choose a password there and then. It needs to be at least 8 characters. After that, signing in is just your email and that password.

So if you are being asked for a code more than once, something has gone wrong. Tell us and we will look.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/guided/login}', '2026-09-05', 'Read the sign-in flow: three steps on one screen. The email-and-code path is only for a first sign-in or a forgotten password; returning founders use email and password. Minimum password length is 8.', NULL, NULL, 'group-21-signing-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('250', '21', 'signing-in', 'Signing in', 'My code hasn''t arrived.', 'Give it a minute, then try these in order.

Check your spam or junk folder. That is where it is most of the time.

Check the email address you typed. One wrong letter and the code has gone somewhere else.

Then press Resend. The button unlocks 60 seconds after the last one, so if it looks disabled, wait a moment.

The code is 8 digits. If what arrived is shorter, it is not from us.

If nothing comes after two tries, write to info@goxl.in from the address you are trying to use, and we will sort it out.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/guided/login}', '2026-09-05', 'Resend cooldown is 60 seconds, matching the mail provider''s own minimum interval so the button never unlocks while sending is still refused. This project issues 8-digit codes.', NULL, NULL, 'group-21-signing-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('251', '21', 'signing-in', 'Signing in', 'The code expired before I could use it.', 'That is fine. Just ask for a new one.

Go back to the sign-in screen, type your email again, and press the button to send a code. A fresh one arrives and the old one stops working.

Codes are deliberately short-lived. It is what stops an old email in your inbox being useful to anyone else later.

One thing worth knowing: always use the newest code. If you have two emails from us, the older code will not work, and it is easy to open the wrong one.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/guided/login}', '2026-09-05', 'Requesting a new code invalidates the previous one. The on-screen copy tells the founder it expires in a few minutes, and this answer deliberately does not print a number the identity provider''s settings could change.', NULL, NULL, 'group-21-signing-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('252', '21', 'signing-in', 'Signing in', 'I signed up with the wrong email address.', 'You cannot change it yourself, so please write to us and we will do it.

Send a message to info@goxl.in. Tell us the wrong address you used and the right one you want, and send it from an address we can recognise.

We do it by hand on purpose. The email is what proves an account is yours, so it is not something a form should change quietly.

If you have not done anything in the account yet, the simpler route is to sign up again with the correct address and tell us to remove the first one.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Live-checked: /settings/account accepts preferred_language and nothing else. The schema states plainly that email and plan are owned by auth and billing and are not editable by the founder.', NULL, NULL, 'group-21-signing-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('253', '21', 'signing-in', 'Signing in', 'I got an email saying someone signed in. Was that me?', 'Quite possibly yes, if it was a device you had not used before.

Ally now emails you when your account is opened from a new device. It tells you what the device was and when. If it was you, there is nothing to do.

If it was not you, change your password. Open Ally the way you normally do, by typing our address into your browser, and use "forgot password" on the sign-in screen.

Our email will never contain a link for that. So if the email you got asks you to click something, it is not from us. Please forward it to info@goxl.in.

You can turn these off in Profile.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Built and tested on 2026-09-05. Live test: first device learned silently, same device again no email, same device on a different address in the same network no email, genuinely new device flagged. The email carries no link on purpose, so ''our emails never ask you to click'' stays true and remains a usable test for phishing.', 'This answer is only safe while it stays true. If sign-in notification emails are ever switched on, this answer becomes dangerous advice and must be rewritten the same day.', 'REPLACES the previous answer, which said we never send sign-in emails and that any such email was phishing. That was true until today and would have become dangerous advice the moment this shipped.', 'group-21-signing-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('254', '21', 'signing-in', 'Signing in', 'It keeps signing me out.', 'This should be fixed now. If it is still happening to you, please tell us.

The cause was having Ally open in more than one tab. The tabs could trip over each other while renewing your session, and one of them would lose and sign you out. That is sorted.

Two other things can still end a session early. Your browser may be set to clear its data when you close it. And private or incognito windows forget everything on purpose.

Otherwise you stay signed in for 30 days on your own computer.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Fixed 2026-09-05 with a cross-tab lock in services/api.js, and verified with two real browser tabs reloading at the same moment with no access token: one took the lock and refreshed, the other waited and reused the result. Zero 401s, neither signed out. The same test produced a revoked-token 401 before the fix.', NULL, NULL, 'group-21-signing-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('255', '21', 'signing-in', 'Signing in', 'Can I stay signed in on my own machine?', 'Yes, and you already are.

On your own computer Ally keeps you signed in for 30 days without asking again. You do not have to tick anything.

Behind the scenes it renews itself quietly while you use it, which is why you can close the tab, come back tomorrow, and still be there.

Two things end it early: signing out, and a browser set to clear its data when it closes.

On a shared or public computer, please do sign out when you finish.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Access tokens last 30 minutes and are renewed automatically from an HttpOnly refresh cookie that lasts 30 days.', NULL, NULL, 'group-21-signing-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('256', '21', 'signing-in', 'Signing in', 'Can I have it open in two tabs at once?', 'Yes, that is fine now.

There used to be a fault where two tabs could trip over each other and sign you out of one of them. It is fixed.

Both tabs share the same session, so you stay signed in on both, and anything you save in one appears in the other when it next loads.

If you do get signed out with two tabs open, that is worth telling us about, because it should not happen any more.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/report}', '2026-09-05', 'Verified with two real tabs reloading simultaneously: one refreshed the session, the other picked up the shared token. Zero 401s, neither tab signed out.', NULL, NULL, 'group-21-signing-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('257', '22', 'settings-and-preferences', 'Settings and preferences', 'What does the notifications toggle actually control?', 'There is no notifications switch on your Profile any more. We took it out.

It did not do anything. There are no in-app notifications for it to turn off, so whichever way you set it, Ally behaved the same. Rather than leave a switch that does nothing, we removed it.

What does reach you has not changed. Ally shows anything overdue when you open it, and if you have connected a calendar, your tasks are on there with proper reminders.

When there is something real to switch off, the switch will come back.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Hidden on 2026-09-05 and verified live: the Preferences card now shows two switches, Call reminders by email and Reduced motion, both of which genuinely work.', NULL, 'Team decision, 2026-09-05.', 'group-22-settings-and-preferences.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('258', '22', 'settings-and-preferences', 'Settings and preferences', 'What is "private mode", and what happens to my data if I leave it off?', 'There is no private mode any more. We removed it, because it did nothing.

The switch claimed to keep your business data anonymised in aggregate insights. Nothing read it, so turning it on or off changed absolutely nothing about how your data was handled. A privacy control that does not control anything is worse than not having one, so it is gone.

What is actually true: your own answers, report and conversations are never used to train anything and are never in any searchable index. We may use anonymous, combined information -- patterns across many founders, with nothing traceable to you -- to improve Ally.

That applies to everybody. It was never something the switch changed.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile,/privacy,/terms}', '2026-09-05', 'Removed from the Profile page and the settings schema on 2026-09-05 and verified live -- the page now shows two switches and the words ''private mode'' and ''aggregate insights'' appear nowhere on it. The data position is the team''s settled one, matching Terms section 4 and Privacy Policy sections 3(c) and 6.', NULL, 'REWRITTEN after the team settled the aggregate-data question on 2026-09-05. An earlier draft said the data ''was never going into anything of the kind'', which was true of the switch but not of the Terms. The honest version separates the two: the switch was empty, and the aggregate use is real but anonymous.', 'group-22-settings-and-preferences.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('259', '22', 'settings-and-preferences', 'Settings and preferences', 'What are these "aggregate insights" my business is going into?', 'It means patterns, not your business.

Our Terms allow us to use anonymous, combined information to improve Ally -- things like which kinds of problem tend to sit underneath which symptoms, across many founders at once. Nothing in it can be traced back to you, your company or anything you wrote.

Your own material is never part of that. Your answers, your report and your conversations are not used to train anything, and are not in any searchable index.

The switch that used to mention this has been removed, because it did not actually control anything. The full wording is in our Terms and Privacy Policy.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile,/privacy,/terms}', '2026-09-05', 'Team''s settled position, 2026-09-05: the Terms and Privacy Policy are the authority. Terms section 4, Privacy Policy sections 3(c) and 6. Separately verified in code that no founder-owned table carries an embedding column, so founder text is never vectorised.', NULL, 'REWRITTEN. An earlier draft said aggregate insights did not exist, which was true of the product but contradicted our own Terms. The team''s call was that the Terms are right.', 'group-22-settings-and-preferences.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('260', '22', 'settings-and-preferences', 'Settings and preferences', 'Can I choose what time Ally reminds me?', 'No, there is no reminder time to set. Ally does not send timed reminders at all.

What you can control is your calendar. Connect it from Plan Your Day and your tasks go in with a reminder half an hour before, which you can then move around in your own calendar however you like.

A task with a date but no time is put at 9 in the morning, so the reminder lands early in the day rather than late the night before.

If you would like Ally itself to remind you at a time you choose, tell us. We are keeping a list.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/plan}', '2026-09-05', 'The reminder settings were removed from the product on 2026-09-05 (team decision) -- they persisted and nothing read them. The 9am default described here is the calendar sync''s own default hour, which is real and working.', NULL, 'Team decision, 2026-09-05. Was ''not yet''; now it is a plain no.', 'group-22-settings-and-preferences.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('261', '22', 'settings-and-preferences', 'Settings and preferences', 'Can I keep goal reminders but turn task reminders off?', 'No. Goals and tasks do not send reminders, so there is nothing to separate.

The only reminder switch in Ally is on your Profile -- "Call reminders by email" -- and it covers reminders before a discovery call you have booked.

What goals and tasks do instead is show up when you open Ally, and go into your calendar if you have connected one. If you want those quieter, your calendar is the place to change it.

If separate reminders would be useful, tell us which ones you would actually want.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'The separate task_reminders and goal_reminders flags were removed on 2026-09-05 (team decision) -- neither was read by anything and neither was reachable in the UI. The email switch on Profile is now the only reminder control that exists.', NULL, 'Team decision, 2026-09-05.', 'group-22-settings-and-preferences.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('262', '22', 'settings-and-preferences', 'Settings and preferences', 'Will Ally email me, or only notify me inside the app?', 'Almost everything happens inside the app. We send very little email.

There are two. When you book a discovery call, you get an email confirming the time with the joining link. And if your account is opened from a device you have not used before, we let you know.

That is all. No daily emails, no weekly summaries, no marketing.

If you have connected a calendar, your task reminders come from your calendar rather than from us.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/discovery-call}', '2026-09-05', 'The only two founder-facing emails in the product are the discovery call booking confirmation and, as of 2026-09-05, the new-device sign-in notice. Call reminders exist and are now schedulable, and no marketing email exists anywhere.', NULL, NULL, 'group-22-settings-and-preferences.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('263', '22', 'settings-and-preferences', 'Settings and preferences', 'How do I stop all email from you?', 'There is very little to stop, but here is what there is.

Go to Profile, then Preferences, and turn off "Call reminders by email". That covers reminders before a discovery call.

Two we would rather you kept. The confirmation when you book a call, because it has the joining link and losing it costs you the call. And the note when your account is opened from a new device, because that is the one that tells you if somebody else is in your account.

We send no marketing email at all, so there is no newsletter to leave.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Verified: the email switch gates only the discovery call reminders. The booking confirmation is transactional. The new-device notice respects the login_notifications preference, which is on by default.', NULL, NULL, 'group-22-settings-and-preferences.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('264', '22', 'settings-and-preferences', 'Settings and preferences', 'Can I replay the tour later?', 'Yes, any time.

Go to Profile and find Product tour under Preferences, then click Replay tour.

The tour walks you through the whole app in 14 short steps. It starts at your Compass and covers each section.

You do not have to finish it. There is a Skip button on every step, and you can stop whenever you like.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Walked: the Replay tour control sits under Preferences on the Profile page and restarts the 14-step guided tour.', NULL, NULL, 'group-22-settings-and-preferences.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('265', '22', 'settings-and-preferences', 'Settings and preferences', 'Does reduced motion change anything besides animations?', 'Yes, a little more than the name suggests.

When you turn it on, Ally stops almost all movement. Things that used to slide, fade or pop will just appear. Long smooth scrolling stops too, so pages jump straight to where you asked to go.

Nothing is hidden and nothing stops working. You can still reach every page and every button. Only the movement changes.

Ally also follows your device setting. If you have turned on ''Reduce motion'' on your phone or computer, Ally is already calm and you do not need this switch.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Tested live earlier in this workstream: turning it on flattened 452 animated elements and turning it off restored them. The device''s own preference is honoured on load.', NULL, NULL, 'group-22-settings-and-preferences.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('266', '22', 'settings-and-preferences', 'Settings and preferences', 'Can I make the text bigger?', 'Use your browser''s zoom. On Windows hold Ctrl and press the plus key, and on a Mac hold Command and press plus. Ctrl or Command with zero puts it back.

That scales the whole page, and Ally is built to reflow properly when you do, so nothing runs off the side.

Being straight with you: your browser''s separate "text size only" setting will not do much in Ally at the moment. Most of our text is set at a fixed size, so that control mostly passes it by. Zoom is the one that works.

We know, and it is on our list.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Measured: of 107 sampled elements, only 7 changed when the root font size was doubled. The app is almost entirely px-based, so text-only scaling has little effect. Page zoom scales everything and the layout reflows without overflow.', 'Text-only scaling is close to a no-op because the styling is px-based throughout. Not a blocker, but it is an accessibility gap and the answer admits it rather than dodging.', NULL, 'group-22-settings-and-preferences.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('267', '22', 'settings-and-preferences', 'Settings and preferences', 'Does this work with a screen reader, or by keyboard only?', 'Mostly yes, and we have just made one part better.

Every page has a proper heading, a skip link so you can jump past the menu, labels on every field, and descriptions on every image. You can move through the app with the Tab key and use buttons with Enter or Space.

Until today the four switches on your Profile were announced as just "button", with no name and no on-or-off state. That is fixed. They now say what they are and whether they are on.

We have not had Ally formally tested for accessibility. If something does not work for you, please tell us and we will fix it.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Audited the Profile page live: 1 main, 1 nav, 1 h1, a skip link present, zero images without alt, zero unlabelled form fields. The only failures were the four switches, fixed in this session and re-verified -- the page now reports zero unnamed controls.', NULL, 'Deliberately does not claim WCAG conformance. Nothing has been formally audited, so the answer says what was checked and admits what was not.', 'group-22-settings-and-preferences.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('268', '22', 'settings-and-preferences', 'Settings and preferences', 'Is there a dark mode?', 'Not yet. Ally is light only at the moment.

If you have your phone or computer set to dark, Ally will not follow it. There is no switch hidden anywhere either, so you are not missing it.

What we do have is reduced motion, under Preferences on your Profile, which helps if the movement rather than the brightness is the problem.

Quite a few people have asked for dark mode. If you would use it, tell us on the Feedback page. It genuinely helps us decide what to build next.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile,/app/feedback}', '2026-09-05', 'Confirmed: zero prefers-color-scheme colour rules are loaded on the app''s pages, and the root element carries no data-theme. There is no dark stylesheet to switch to.', NULL, NULL, 'group-22-settings-and-preferences.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('269', '23', 'your-data-rights-in-detail', 'Your data rights, in detail', 'What''s the difference between "download my data" and "export for portability"?', 'They give you two different files.

"Download my data" gives you everything we hold. That includes what Ally worked out about you -- your reports, the root causes it found, and what it remembers about your business.

"Export for portability" gives you only what you gave us. Your answers, your goals, your tasks, your conversations and your profile. It leaves out Ally''s own analysis, because that is the part you would not be taking anywhere else.

Both are JSON files, both download straight away, and both are in Profile, then Privacy Center.

If you just want a copy of everything, use the first one.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Ran both: access returns 23 sections and 183 records; portability returns 11 sections and 126 records, covering only founder-supplied data.', NULL, NULL, 'group-23-your-data-rights-in-detail.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('270', '23', 'your-data-rights-in-detail', 'Your data rights, in detail', 'What does "view data summary" show me?', 'It shows how much we hold, not what it says.

You get counts, grouped into six plain headings: your profile and settings, your diagnosis, your reports and what Ally worked out, your conversations, your goals and tasks, and your account record.

It appears on screen. Nothing downloads, and nothing changes.

It is meant as a quick look before you decide whether to download the full thing. If you want to read the actual data, use "Download my data" on the same page.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Ran it: 186 records grouped into six categories plus a catch-all, and the categories reconcile to the total so a new kind of record cannot quietly go missing.', NULL, NULL, 'group-23-your-data-rights-in-detail.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('271', '23', 'your-data-rights-in-detail', 'Your data rights, in detail', 'I want a fact corrected. Will that change my report?', 'We will correct the fact. Your report will not change.

Use "Request data correction" in the Privacy Center and tell us what is wrong and what it should say. A person reads it and fixes the record.

Your report is different. It was written from your answers on the day you did the diagnosis, and it stays as it was -- a record of that moment, not a live document. Correcting a fact now does not rewrite it, and we will not pretend it does.

If the fact was central to what Ally concluded, say so in the request. That is worth a conversation rather than a correction.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', '''Request data correction'' is the one Privacy Center action that queues for a human. Reports are immutable once generated -- nothing anywhere regenerates one, consistent with answer 69.', NULL, NULL, 'group-23-your-data-rights-in-detail.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('272', '23', 'your-data-rights-in-detail', 'Your data rights, in detail', 'What does "restrict data processing" stop, exactly?', 'It stops Ally thinking about you, and nothing else.

While it is on, you cannot send messages to Ally or start a diagnosis. Both stop with a notice telling you to resume from the Privacy Center.

Everything you already have stays exactly as it is. Your account is active, your report is readable, your goals and tasks are all there, and nothing is deleted.

It is a pause, not a decision. You can turn it back on whenever you like and it takes effect straight away.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Tested live: with processing restricted, a chat message returns a clear refusal naming the Privacy Center. Nothing stored is affected and resuming restores normal function immediately.', NULL, NULL, 'group-23-your-data-rights-in-detail.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('273', '23', 'your-data-rights-in-detail', 'Your data rights, in detail', 'What''s the difference between restricting processing and withdrawing consent?', 'One is a pause. The other is a decision.

Restricting processing is a switch. Ally stops analysing anything new until you turn it back on. Use it if you want a break, or you are thinking something over.

Withdrawing consent takes away our permission to analyse your data at all. It is the formal version, and it is your right under the law.

In practice they stop the same things: no new chat, no new diagnosis. Neither deletes anything, and neither closes your account.

If you are unsure which you want, restrict processing. It is the reversible one.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Both surface in the Privacy Center and both block the same two operations. Neither deletes anything or deactivates the account. The right to withdraw consent is section 7(e) of the published Privacy Policy.', NULL, NULL, 'group-23-your-data-rights-in-detail.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('274', '23', 'your-data-rights-in-detail', 'Your data rights, in detail', 'If I withdraw consent, do I lose my report?', 'No. Your report stays and you can still read it.

Withdrawing consent stops new analysis. It does not delete anything you already have. Your report, your Founder DNA, your goals and your past conversations are all still there.

What stops is Ally doing anything new with your data -- no new messages, no new diagnosis.

If you want the report gone as well, that is account deletion, which is a separate action on the same page and has a 30-day window before it becomes permanent.

And if you change your mind, you can give consent again.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile,/app/report}', '2026-09-05', 'Withdrawing consent revokes the basis for new processing and leaves every existing record intact. Deletion is a separate action with its own 30-day grace window.', NULL, NULL, 'group-23-your-data-rights-in-detail.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('275', '23', 'your-data-rights-in-detail', 'Your data rights, in detail', 'I paused processing. How do I start it again?', 'Go to Profile, then Privacy Center. There is an amber banner at the top with a Resume button.

Press it and Ally starts working normally again straight away. There is no waiting and nothing to confirm.

If you cannot see the banner, you are probably not paused any more -- try sending Ally a message and see whether it answers.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Tested live: the amber banner carries a Resume control and lifting the restriction restores chat and diagnosis immediately.', NULL, NULL, 'group-23-your-data-rights-in-detail.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('276', '23', 'your-data-rights-in-detail', 'Your data rights, in detail', 'I scheduled deletion by mistake. Can I stop it?', 'Yes, and you can do it yourself. Just sign in.

While your deletion is scheduled, signing in shows you a message about it with a button that says "Cancel deletion & continue". Press that and your account carries on as normal.

Nothing has been erased in the meantime. The 30-day window exists precisely so a mis-click is recoverable.

You do not need to email anybody. If the button does not work for you, then write to us -- but it should.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Verified: DeletionPendingGate is mounted in PlatformLayout and shows a blocking prompt with a one-click ''Cancel deletion & continue'' during the grace window.', NULL, 'The question bank recorded this as ''no self-serve cancel, the banner says contact support''. That was true of the COPY, which has since been corrected -- the button itself has existed throughout.', 'group-23-your-data-rights-in-detail.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('277', '23', 'your-data-rights-in-detail', 'Your data rights, in detail', 'How long do I have to change my mind?', 'Thirty days from the day you ask for deletion.

Until that date your account works completely normally and nothing has been removed. Sign in any time before it and you will be offered the chance to cancel.

After that date it is permanent. Your data is erased or made anonymous, and it cannot be brought back.

Two things outlive it, and only because the law requires it: financial records are kept for seven years, and anything already made anonymous -- which cannot be traced back to you -- may be kept.

If you want a copy of anything, download it before the date.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Matches the published Privacy Policy section 6 word for word: erasure or anonymisation within 30 days, financial records retained 7 years under Indian law, anonymised data retained indefinitely.', NULL, NULL, 'group-23-your-data-rights-in-detail.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('278', '23', 'your-data-rights-in-detail', 'Your data rights, in detail', 'Is Ally actually DPDP and GDPR compliant, or just saying so?', 'DPDP yes. GDPR does not apply to us, and we would rather say so than imply it.

Our Privacy Policy is written to India''s Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023 and the IT Act 2000. That is not just a sentence: the rights it gives you are built and working. You can download your data, export it, ask for a correction, pause processing, withdraw consent and delete your account, all from the Privacy Center, and most happen immediately.

We also name a Grievance Officer, which the DPDP Act requires.

Ally is for founders in India at the moment, which is why GDPR is not something we claim.

We have not been independently audited. If you need that for a compliance review, ask us and we will tell you exactly where we stand.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile,/privacy}', '2026-09-06', 'Team decision 2026-09-06: DPDP only, and users are India-based for now, so GDPR is deliberately out of scope. Privacy Policy claims DPDP 2023 and IT Act 2000 and names a Grievance Officer. Every right listed was exercised during the walk.', NULL, 'Team decision, 2026-09-06.', 'group-23-your-data-rights-in-detail.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('279', '23', 'your-data-rights-in-detail', 'Your data rights, in detail', 'You say requests are reviewed within 30 days. Why does it take that long?', 'For most things it does not. Thirty days is the legal maximum, not our normal speed.

Downloading your data, exporting it, viewing the summary, pausing processing and withdrawing consent all happen the moment you press the button. Nothing waits for anybody.

The one that genuinely needs a person is a data correction, because somebody has to check what is wrong and fix the right record. Those are usually done in a few days.

The thirty days is there so that a hard request, or one that arrives while somebody is away, still has a promise attached to it.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'Walked all seven Privacy Center actions: six are served immediately, and only ''Request data correction'' queues for a human.', NULL, NULL, 'group-23-your-data-rights-in-detail.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('280', '24', 'ownership-and-the-long-term', 'Ownership and the long term', 'Who owns my report -- me, or GoXL?', 'The contents are yours. The format is ours.

Everything you put in -- your answers, your business information, what you told Ally -- you own outright. Our terms say so plainly, and we only get permission to use it to run the service for you.

What belongs to us is the thing around it: the framework, the way the report is laid out, and the platform itself.

In practice this matters less than it sounds. It is your report, you can download it, keep it and read it forever. If you want to use it in something you are sending outside your business, see the next answer.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/terms,/app/report}', '2026-09-05', 'Terms section 4 (''You retain full ownership of all business information, diagnostic inputs, and data you provide'') read against section 6 (the Platform, its models, report formats and design are GoXL''s property).', NULL, NULL, 'group-24-ownership-and-the-long-term.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('281', '24', 'ownership-and-the-long-term', 'Ownership and the long term', 'Can I use what Ally gives me commercially -- in a pitch, in an investor deck?', 'Yes. It is your report and your business -- use it however you like.

Put it in an investor deck, take it into a board meeting, share the whole thing or a single page. That is your call, and we are not going to tell you what to do with a document about your own company.

One practical thought rather than a rule: a report reads as a report. In a deck it usually lands better if you take the finding and put it in your own words and your own slides. But that is a presentation opinion, not a restriction.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/report}', '2026-09-06', 'Team decision 2026-09-06: a founder''s use of their own report is their personal choice. Terms section 4 already gives the founder full ownership of their business information and diagnostic inputs.', NULL, 'Team decision, 2026-09-06. Earlier drafts hedged on Terms section 6''s ''internal business purposes only''. The team''s position is that the report is the founder''s to use, so the hedge is gone.', 'group-24-ownership-and-the-long-term.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('282', '24', 'ownership-and-the-long-term', 'Ownership and the long term', 'Can I quote Ally''s report to a client of mine?', 'Yes, go ahead.

The findings are about your business, so quoting them to a client is entirely your call. Share a line, a section, or the whole report if it helps.

The one thing that is different is reselling. Using Ally as part of a service you charge clients for -- running diagnoses for them, packaging the reports as your own product -- needs a conversation with us first. That is not a no, it just is not automatic.

Write to info@goxl.in if that is what you have in mind.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/terms,/app/help}', '2026-09-06', 'Team decision 2026-09-06. Terms section 5(f) still prohibits reselling or sublicensing access without prior written consent, which is a different thing from a founder quoting their own report.', NULL, 'Team decision, 2026-09-06.', 'group-24-ownership-and-the-long-term.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('283', '24', 'ownership-and-the-long-term', 'Ownership and the long term', 'What are you allowed to do with what I write?', 'Use it to run Ally for you, and to make Ally better in a way that is not about you.

Our terms give us a limited licence to process your data solely to deliver the service -- to build your report, to let Ally answer you properly, and to keep your account working.

We do not sell it. We do not rent it. We do not share it with anyone for advertising or marketing.

We also use anonymous, combined information -- patterns across many founders, with nothing that could point back to you -- to improve Ally. Your own writing is never used to train anything, and is never in any searchable index.

It is all in the Terms if you want the full wording.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/terms,/privacy}', '2026-09-05', 'Terms section 4. The aggregate half is the team''s settled position as of 2026-09-05 and matches Privacy Policy sections 3(c) and 6. Consistent with answer 206.', NULL, 'Team decision, 2026-09-05.', 'group-24-ownership-and-the-long-term.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('284', '24', 'ownership-and-the-long-term', 'Ownership and the long term', 'Can you close my account? On what grounds?', 'We can, and the grounds are in our terms rather than at our whim.

The short version: breaking the rules. Trying to get into someone else''s account, deliberately giving false business information, scraping or reverse-engineering the platform, reselling access, or using Ally for something unlawful.

We are not going to close your account for disagreeing with your report, complaining, or asking for a refund.

If we ever did suspend an account, you would be able to ask why and get a straight answer at info@goxl.in.

In practice this has not happened, and the clause exists for the obvious cases rather than the borderline ones.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/terms,/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Terms section 3 (suspend or terminate accounts that violate the Terms) and section 5 (the list of prohibited conduct). Section 8 covers termination and what survives it.', NULL, NULL, 'group-24-ownership-and-the-long-term.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('285', '24', 'ownership-and-the-long-term', 'Ownership and the long term', 'What happens to my report if GoXL shuts down or gets bought?', NULL, 'policy', 'retired', 'false', NULL, '{}', '2026-09-06', 'Retired by team decision 2026-09-06.', NULL, 'RETIRED, not unanswered. The team''s position is that this is not a question to put in front of founders at launch. It stays in the bank with its id so nobody re-adds it by accident, and is excluded from the export. If a founder does ask, support answers it individually.', 'group-24-ownership-and-the-long-term.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('286', '24', 'ownership-and-the-long-term', 'Ownership and the long term', 'You changed the terms. Do I have to accept?', 'Not by signing anything. Carrying on using Ally is what counts as accepting.

When something important changes, we tell you -- through the app or by email -- before it takes effect. For the Privacy Policy that is at least seven days'' notice.

If you are not happy with a change, the honest options are to tell us, or to stop using Ally and delete your account. There is no way to stay on the old terms.

The date and version are always at the top of the Terms page, so you can see what you are on.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/terms,/privacy}', '2026-09-05', 'Terms section 10 (material changes notified via the Platform or email; continued use constitutes acceptance; version and effective date shown at the top). Privacy Policy section 11 specifies at least 7 days'' notice.', NULL, NULL, 'group-24-ownership-and-the-long-term.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('287', '24', 'ownership-and-the-long-term', 'Ownership and the long term', 'Is there a minimum age?', 'Yes. You need to be at least 18.

Our terms require it, and you also have to be able to enter into an agreement for yourself or for your business.

There is no separate account type for anyone younger, and no plans for one.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/terms}', '2026-09-05', 'Terms section 1: at least 18 years old, with the legal authority to enter the agreement.', NULL, NULL, 'group-24-ownership-and-the-long-term.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('288', '24', 'ownership-and-the-long-term', 'Ownership and the long term', 'If something goes wrong, whose law applies and where?', 'Indian law, and the courts in Bangalore.

Our terms say any dispute is governed by the laws of India, and that the courts of Bangalore, Karnataka have exclusive jurisdiction.

Before anything reaches a court, both sides are expected to try to sort it out properly first. If it is still unresolved after 30 days, then it can go further.

For anything short of that -- a complaint, a bill you think is wrong, a report you are unhappy with -- write to info@goxl.in. Almost everything is settled there.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/terms,/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Terms section 9: governed by the laws of India, good-faith negotiation first, exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of Bangalore, Karnataka if unresolved within 30 days.', NULL, NULL, 'group-24-ownership-and-the-long-term.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('289', '24', 'ownership-and-the-long-term', 'Ownership and the long term', 'Can I rely on Ally''s advice? Are you liable if it''s wrong?', 'Use it to think with. Do not use it as professional advice, and the decision stays yours.

Our terms are direct about this: Ally is a decision-support tool, not legal, financial or management consulting advice, and you remain responsible for what you decide.

On liability, they are equally direct. Ally is provided as is, with no guarantee that everything it produces is accurate, and if you ever did have a claim against us it is capped at what you have paid us in the previous three months.

We would rather you knew that up front than found it in a clause later.

If Ally gets something wrong about your business, please tell us. That is worth fixing.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/terms,/app/feedback}', '2026-09-05', 'Terms section 2 (decision-support tool, not professional advice, founder solely responsible) and section 7 (AS IS, no warranties as to accuracy, liability capped at three months'' fees, no indirect damages).', NULL, NULL, 'group-24-ownership-and-the-long-term.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('290', '25', 'fit-connections-getting-data-in', 'Fit, connections, getting data in', 'Can I upload my business plan or deck instead of answering all this?', 'No. Every question in the diagnosis has to be answered by you.

That is deliberate, and it is the whole point. Ally is trying to understand you, not just your business -- how you describe things, what you reach for first, where you hesitate. A document tells us about the company. It does not tell us about the founder, and half of what the diagnosis reads is the founder.

Your plan is still useful, though. Upload it in a conversation and Ally will work through it with you, quote your own numbers back and tell you what it makes of them.

The diagnosis takes about half an hour, and you can stop and come back.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/ally-chat,/app/diagnosis}', '2026-09-05', 'Team decision 2026-09-05: the diagnosis will not be pre-filled or shortened from an uploaded document, because the system needs to hear from the founder directly. Chat file reading is unaffected and still works for PDFs, Word, plain text and CSV.', NULL, 'Team decision, 2026-09-05.', 'group-25-fit-connections-getting-data-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('291', '25', 'fit-connections-getting-data-in', 'Fit, connections, getting data in', 'Can Ally connect to my accounting, CRM or bank data?', 'No, and there is no plan to connect to your bank.

Ally works from what you tell it, not from your systems. Nothing is plugged into your accounts.

For what it does, that matters less than you would think. The diagnosis asks for rough figures -- roughly what is coming in, roughly how many customers -- and approximate answers are genuinely fine.

If you want Ally to look at real numbers, export them and upload the file in a conversation. It reads spreadsheets and PDFs, and it can work through your actual figures with you that way.

If a particular connection would change things for you, tell us which one.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/ally-chat}', '2026-09-05', 'Searched the whole repo: no accounting, CRM or banking integration exists. CSV upload in chat is real and was tested -- Ally quoted exact figures from an uploaded file.', NULL, NULL, 'group-25-fit-connections-getting-data-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('292', '25', 'fit-connections-getting-data-in', 'Fit, connections, getting data in', 'Does it work with Notion, Slack, or anything I already use?', 'Not yet. Ally does not connect to Notion, Slack or any other tool.

The one exception is your calendar. Connect it from Plan Your Day and your tasks go into it, so at least the things you decide to do turn up where you already look.

Everything else is copy and paste for now. Your report downloads as a PDF, so it goes into Notion or a Drive folder easily enough.

If there is one tool you would genuinely use this with, tell us which. We are keeping a list, and it is short enough that a few votes decide it.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/plan}', '2026-09-05', 'Google Calendar is the only outbound integration in the product. No Notion, Slack or Zapier code exists anywhere.', NULL, NULL, 'group-25-fit-connections-getting-data-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('293', '25', 'fit-connections-getting-data-in', 'Fit, connections, getting data in', 'Is there an API?', 'No. There is no public API and nothing you can build against.

Ally''s data moves in and out two ways: your report downloads as a PDF, and the Privacy Center gives you a full JSON export of everything we hold, which is machine-readable if you want to do something with it.

For most people that export is the thing they actually wanted.

If you have a real use for an API, please tell us what you would do with it. That is the sort of thing we would build for a reason and not on spec.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'There is no public API surface, no founder-facing API key and no developer documentation. The privacy export is genuine machine-readable JSON.', NULL, 'Deliberately does NOT say ''not yet''. An API is a long-term commitment to a contract, and ''not yet'' from a support bot is how a roadmap promise gets made by accident.', 'group-25-fit-connections-getting-data-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('294', '25', 'fit-connections-getting-data-in', 'Fit, connections, getting data in', 'Can I bring my existing goals in from another tool?', 'Not automatically. There is no import.

You would need to type them in on the Goals page, which is genuinely quick for the handful that matter.

And honestly, that is not the worst thing. Most founders arrive with a list of twenty goals from somewhere else, and the useful exercise is deciding which three are real. Ally is built around a small number of things you are actually going to do.

If you are moving from another tool and have a long list, bring it to a conversation with Ally and work out which ones to keep.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/goals,/app/ally-chat}', '2026-09-05', 'No import path exists for goals or tasks. Goals are created in Ally or come out of the diagnosis.', NULL, NULL, 'group-25-fit-connections-getting-data-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('295', '25', 'fit-connections-getting-data-in', 'Fit, connections, getting data in', 'Can I refer another founder? Do I get anything for it?', 'Please do tell them about us -- but there is no referral scheme, so there is nothing in it for you at the moment. No code to share, no credit, no discount.

What there is: our first 100 founders get benefits and coupons as a thank-you for being early. If you are one of them, that comes to you automatically -- there is nothing to claim.

If a proper referral scheme would make you tell more people, say so. That is the kind of thing that gets built when enough people ask.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/feedback}', '2026-09-06', 'Team decision 2026-09-06: no referral programme; the first 100 users receive benefits and coupons instead. Confirmed that nothing in the repo implements referrals.', 'The first-100 benefit is a promise with no mechanism behind it yet. Nothing in the catalog or the credits system grants anything to early founders automatically. Somebody needs to decide what they get and how it is applied before the 100th signup, not after.', 'Team decision, 2026-09-06.', 'group-25-fit-connections-getting-data-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('296', '25', 'fit-connections-getting-data-in', 'Fit, connections, getting data in', 'I''m a nonprofit / an agency / a one-person practice. Does the model still apply?', 'Mostly yes, with one honest caveat.

Ally is built around a founder and the organisation they are running. That much fits a nonprofit, an agency or a practice of one as well as it fits a startup. The questions about clarity, focus, what only you can decide and what is actually stuck are the same questions.

The caveat is revenue. Some of what Ally looks at assumes money coming from customers. If you are grant-funded, or your income works differently, that part will fit less well and the report will be thinner there.

Everything about you as the person running it applies exactly the same.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/guided/profile}', '2026-09-05', 'The framework is stage-and-business based. Revenue Maturity is one of six pillars and is scoped out at early stages, so a founder without conventional revenue gets a report weighted to the other five rather than a broken one.', NULL, NULL, 'group-25-fit-connections-getting-data-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('297', '25', 'fit-connections-getting-data-in', 'Fit, connections, getting data in', 'My cofounder reads the business completely differently. Can Ally handle that?', 'Not in one account, no. Ally hears one voice -- whoever answered the questions.

So the report reflects how you see the business. If your cofounder would have answered differently, that difference does not appear anywhere, and the report is not the neutral referee between you.

There are two things worth doing. Read the report together and mark where they would have answered differently -- that disagreement is usually more useful than the report itself. And bring it to a discovery call, where a person can hold both readings at once.

A proper two-founder version does not exist yet.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/report,/app/discovery-call}', '2026-09-05', 'One diagnosis per account, answered by one founder. There is no multi-user account, no cofounder access and no way to record a second set of answers. Consistent with answers 31, 200 and 201.', NULL, NULL, 'group-25-fit-connections-getting-data-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('298', '25', 'fit-connections-getting-data-in', 'Fit, connections, getting data in', 'Does this work on slow or patchy internet?', 'Mostly, but it will feel slow in two places.

Ally''s replies arrive a piece at a time, so on a weak connection they come in slowly rather than failing. That part copes.

The two heavy moments are your Compass, which loads a lot at once, and downloading your report as a PDF.

If a page does not load, refreshing usually fixes it. Nothing is lost when a connection drops -- your diagnosis answers are saved one at a time as you send them, so you never go back to the beginning.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app}', '2026-09-05', 'Answers are persisted individually on submit, so a dropped connection costs at most the answer in flight. Compass is the heaviest page in the product and the report PDF is the largest single download.', NULL, NULL, 'group-25-fit-connections-getting-data-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('299', '25', 'fit-connections-getting-data-in', 'Fit, connections, getting data in', 'Does any of it work offline?', 'No. Ally needs a connection for everything.

There is nothing stored on your device to fall back on, so with no internet you will not be able to open it at all.

The one thing you can keep offline is your report. Download it as a PDF and it is yours to read on a plane or anywhere else.

If you know you are going to be without a connection, download it first.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/report}', '2026-09-05', 'No service worker and no PWA manifest exist, so there is no offline capability of any kind. The report PDF is the only artefact a founder can keep locally.', NULL, NULL, 'group-25-fit-connections-getting-data-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
insert into "support_bot_answers" ("question_id", "group_number", "group_slug", "group_title", "question", "answer", "answer_type", "status", "is_published", "blocked_by", "links", "verified_on", "verified_how", "finding", "note", "source_file", "created_at", "updated_at") values ('300', '25', 'fit-connections-getting-data-in', 'Fit, connections, getting data in', 'Everything is in rupees and Indian examples. Does it hold up for a business abroad?', 'The thinking does. The furniture around it is Indian.

What Ally actually measures -- your clarity, your market, how your revenue works, whether too much depends on you -- is not specific to any country. A founder in Berlin gets the same six areas and the same kind of root cause.

What is Indian is the surroundings. Prices are in rupees, support runs on India time, and the case studies behind the framework are Indian businesses. So some examples will feel local.

Nothing checks where you are, so it works wherever you sit. If you are outside India and thinking of paying, write to us first.', 'walked', 'answered', 'true', NULL, '{/app/help}', '2026-09-05', 'Nothing in the scoring, the six pillars or the root-cause rules is geography-dependent. Prices are INR, support hours are IST, and the knowledge base was built from Indian founder case studies. Consistent with answer 234.', NULL, NULL, 'group-25-fit-connections-getting-data-in.json', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00', '2026-09-06 10:46:27.236539+00') on conflict do nothing;
